{"name": "Frodnar", "count": 1}, {"name": "Embry", "count": 1}, {"name": "Nazeem", "count": 1}, {"name": "Fralia Gray-Mane", "count": 1}, {"name": "Jon Battle-Born", "count": 1}, {"name": "Jarl Balgruuf the Greater", "count": 1}, {"name": "Whiterun Guard", "count": 1}, {"name": "Farengar Secret-Fire", "count": 1}, {"name": "Anoriath", "count": 1}, {"name": "Olfina Gray-Mane", "count": 1}, {"name": "Amren", "count": 1}, {"name": "Mila Valentia", "count": 1}, {"name": "Arngeir", "count": 1}, {"name": "Wulfgar", "count": 1}, {"name": "Einarth", "count": 1}, {"name": "Orgnar", "count": 1}, {"name": "Delphine", "count": 1}, {"name": "Dorthe", "count": 1}, {"name": "Sven", "count": 1}, {"name": "Lucia", "count": 1}, {"name": "Mikael", "count": 1}, {"name": "Ysolda", "count": 1}, {"name": "Adrianne Avenicci", "count": 1}, {"name": "Braith", "count": 1}, {"name": "Beirand", "count": 1}, {"name": "Lisette", "count": 1}, {"name": "Jaree-Ra", "count": 1}, {"name": "Fihada", "count": 1}, {"name": "Jordis the Sword-Maiden", "count": 1}, {"name": "Noster Eagle-Eye", "count": 1}, {"name": "Svaknir", "count": 1}, {"name": "Bryling", "count": 1}, {"name": "Melaran", "count": 1}, {"name": "Bolgeir Bearclaw", "count": 1}, {"name": "Jarl Elisif the Fair", "count": 1}, {"name": "Varnius Junius", "count": 1}, {"name": "Erikur", "count": 1}, {"name": "Odar", "count": 1}, {"name": "Sybille Stentor", "count": 1}, {"name": "Falk Firebeard", "count": 1}, {"name": "Erdi", "count": 1}, {"name": "Una", "count": 1}, {"name": "Jorn", "count": 1}, {"name": "Aia Arria", "count": 1}, {"name": "Kayd", "count": 1}, {"name": "Sorex Vinius", "count": 1}, {"name": "Illdi", "count": 1}, {"name": "Bendt", "count": 1}, {"name": "Pantea Ateia", "count": 1}, {"name": "Giraud Gemane", "count": 1}, {"name": "Ancano", "count": 1}, {"name": "J'zargo", "count": 1}, {"name": "Onuja", "count": 1}, {"name": "Sergius Turrianus", "count": 1}, {"name": "Amanra Solas", "count": 1}, {"name": "Nirya", "count": 1}, {"name": "Nelysa", "count": 1}, {"name": "Mirabelle Ervine", "count": 1}, {"name": "Enthir", "count": 1}, {"name": "Tolfdir", "count": 1}, {"name": "Myvrana Giladren", "count": 1}], "memories": [{"id": 5, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "content", "location": "Bleak Falls Barrow Outskirts, Whiterun Hold", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Jules and I fought our way through three bandits — a Redguard, an Orc, and a Wood Elf outlaw — at the outskirts of Bleak Falls Barrow this morning. I dropped the Redguard with my arrows and Jules finished the Orc; the Bosmer outlaw yielded but Jules cut her down anyway. Six arrows spent, three dead. Jules keeps mangling my name — 'FanDoll,' 'Fiendal' — and I've had to correct her twice. We're now at the barrow entrance; she's sent me back from going inside but keeps pulling me along regardless.", "day": "19th of Last Seed", "gt": 213322.56, "x": 0.498, "y": 0.801, "ux": 0.2502, "uy": 0.5946}, {"id": 6, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "content", "location": "Bleak Falls Barrow Outskirts, Whiterun Hold, Outdoors", "imp": 0.65, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Woke at the Sleeping Giant Inn in Riverwood and set out with Faendal — he kept correcting me every time I called him 'FanDoll' — toward Bleak Falls Barrow. On the approach to the barrow's outskirts, we were attacked by three bandits: a Redguard man, an Orc man, and a Wood Elf woman outlaw. Faendal dropped the Redguard with his bow while I finished the Orc; the outlaw tried to yield but I cut her down regardless. After the fight I tried to send Faendal away, then changed my mind and asked him to follow me again — we're now lingering at the barrow's outskirts, the iron door into the ruin still ahead of us.", "day": "19th of Last Seed", "gt": 213322.56, "x": 0.7908, "y": 0.1589, "ux": 0.235, "uy": 0.7648}, {"id": 7, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Bleak Falls Barrow, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.75, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In Bleak Falls Barrow, I fought through bandits and skeevers alongside Faendal, killing several in tight corridors. I helped defeat a wounded frostbite spider that had Arvel the Swift trapped in webbing. Afterward, Arvel begged us to free him, claiming the Golden Claw was his and promising rewards. I remain wary of his motives but now have the Claw in my possession.", "day": "20th of Last Seed", "gt": 292295.1, "x": 0.8605, "y": 0.3408, "ux": 0.2373, "uy": 0.7085}, {"id": 8, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Bleak Falls Barrow, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.65, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought bandits inside Bleak Falls Barrow with Jules, killed a skeever in the dark tunnels, and encountered Arvel the Swift trapped in spiderwebbing. Arvel claims he stole the Golden Claw from Lucan's shop in Riverwood and offers it as thanks for freeing him. Jules keeps misnaming me—Faendal, not 'Fandock'—but pushes forward despite the danger.", "day": "20th of Last Seed", "gt": 292295.1, "x": 0.7058, "y": 0.5675, "ux": 0.245, "uy": 0.692}, {"id": 9, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Bleak Falls Barrow, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.75, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In Bleak Falls Barrow, Faendal and I fought through waves of draugr, including a Restless Draugr he felled with precise arrows. Arvel the Swift betrayed us, claiming the Golden Claw was his, but Faendal killed him when he drew a blade. I retrieved Arvel's journal and a Nord warhammer, deciding to sell it at War Maidens in Whiterun for better coin. Despite tensions, Faendal proved a capable ally in the tomb's depths.", "day": "20th of Last Seed", "gt": 299267.37, "x": 0.9389, "y": 0.395, "ux": 0.2247, "uy": 0.7198}, {"id": 10, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Bleak Falls Barrow, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.75, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In Bleak Falls Barrow, Arvel the Swift betrayed us after being freed from spiderwebs, threatening to keep the Golden Claw for himself. I killed him when he drew his blade, judging him too dangerous to trust. Jules questioned the swiftness of the execution, but I reminded her dead men tell no tales. We pressed deeper into the barrow, fighting multiple draugr, with me taking down at least four using my bow and blade.", "day": "20th of Last Seed", "gt": 299267.37, "x": 0.8467, "y": 0.483, "ux": 0.2358, "uy": 0.7031}, {"id": 11, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Bleak Falls Barrow, Hall of Stories, Whiterun Hold", "imp": 0.85, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In the Hall of Stories within Bleak Falls Barrow, Faendal and I faced a Draugr Overlord. The creature unleashed a powerful shout that staggered me, but Faendal felled it with a well-placed arrow. I recovered against the wall, wounded but alive, and we prepared to continue toward Whiterun. I decided to sell the Nord warhammer and Golden Claw at War Maidens to fund my journey to Solitude.", "day": "20th of Last Seed", "gt": 310506.84, "x": 0.9081, "y": 0.366, "ux": 0.2294, "uy": 0.7203}, {"id": 12, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Bleak Falls Barrow, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.85, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In Bleak Falls Barrow, I fought alongside Jules through bandits, draugr, and finally the Draugr Overlord, which I killed with a decisive strike after it shouted at us. Arvel the Swift betrayed us earlier, but I ended him swiftly—trust is a luxury in tombs. Jules questioned my methods, but survival comes before sentiment. I kept my bow ready throughout, looted linen wraps near a chest, and agreed to carry our spoils to Whiterun's War Maiden for sale. Mentioned Camilla Valerius subtly, testing Jules' familiarity, but she seemed distracted by the aftermath.", "day": "20th of Last Seed", "gt": 310506.84, "x": 0.7256, "y": 0.6643, "ux": 0.2482, "uy": 0.6307}, {"id": 13, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "content", "location": "Whiterun Khajiit Caravan, Outdoors, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.75, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Journeyed from Riverwood to Whiterun with Jules after escaping Bleak Falls Barrow, where we fought bandits and draugr, including killing Arvel the Swift and the Draugr Overlord. Mentioned Camilla Valerius during our travel but received little response. Passed through the wilderness and Whiterun Military Camp, staying vigilant for threats. Currently arriving near the Whiterun Khajiit Caravan with Jules, still carrying my bow and firewood.", "day": "20th of Last Seed", "gt": 320842.67, "x": 0.8149, "y": 0.6735, "ux": 0.217, "uy": 0.655}, {"id": 14, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Riverwood, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.75, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Emerging from Bleak Falls Barrow with Faendal after defeating the Draugr Overlord, we made our way toward Riverwood. Dorthe greeted me near Alvor's house, unafraid and defiant of her father's warnings. Faendal and I continued toward Whiterun, cutting through the valley past the military camp with the Khajiit caravan in sight. I'm wounded but full of magic, determined to reach Whiterun before nightfall and sell the Golden Claw and Nord warhammer to fund my journey to Solitude.", "day": "20th of Last Seed", "gt": 320842.67, "x": 0.9107, "y": 0.2802, "ux": 0.2178, "uy": 0.7048}, {"id": 15, "actor": "Ulfberth War-Bear", "emotion": "content", "location": "Warmaiden's, near the Door to Whiterun, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Traded with the Breton adventurer at Warmaiden's near Whiterun's main gate, buying several weapons and two steel spears for 151 gold total. Recognized her from a previous browse — steel armor, crossbow, looks like a fighter. Faendal the Bosmer hunter came in right after, eyeing wares with coin in hand. Business is good this morning.", "day": "20th of Last Seed", "gt": 330370.54, "x": 0.9504, "y": 0.3562, "ux": 0.222, "uy": 0.6379}, {"id": 16, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Bannered Mare in Whiterun", "imp": 0.55, "type": "RELATIONSHIP", "content": "In the Bannered Mare, Olfina Gray-Mane questions my presence as Jules's companion, sizing me up with sharp eyes. I deflect with a half-truth about hunting work and leaving Riverwood's mill behind, keeping my bow close. Her Stormcloak leanings are obvious, but I stay neutral—gold and survival matter more than politics.", "day": "20th of Last Seed", "gt": 329081.22, "x": 0.6397, "y": 0.6109, "ux": 0.1075, "uy": 0.5649}, {"id": 17, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "content", "location": "The Bannered Mare in Whiterun", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Sold the Nord warhammer and other loot to Ulfberth War-Bear at Warmaiden's in Whiterun for 151 gold total. Rented a room at the Bannered Mare for 75 gold and bought food from Saadia, spending 204 gold. Hulda mentioned wanting to retire and sell the inn to Ysolda. Overheard Mikael performing songs praising the Imperials while Jon Battle-Born and Olfina Gray-Mane were present. Woke the next morning rested, remembering I must deliver the Dragonstone to Farengar in Dragonsreach.", "day": "20th of Last Seed", "gt": 329081.22, "x": 0.7988, "y": 0.2919, "ux": 0.2005, "uy": 0.6865}, {"id": 18, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "content", "location": "Lucan's Dry Goods, near the Wooden Door to Riverwood, Hold: Riverwood", "imp": 0.7, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Delivered the Golden Claw to Lucan Valerius at his shop in Riverwood, fulfilling his request. He expressed deep gratitude, calling it a great thing for him and his sister Camilla. I purchased four Potions of Minor Healing and one of Minor Stamina, spending 325 gold despite having only 261, implying a debt or error. Bade farewell to Faendal, who joked about the dragonstone as he returned to the mill.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 368971.83, "x": 0.8332, "y": 0.2704, "ux": 0.1932, "uy": 0.687}, {"id": 19, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Lucan's Dry Goods, near the Wooden Door to Riverwood, Hold: Riverwood", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Standing with Jules at Lucan's Dry Goods in Riverwood after returning the Golden Claw. Lucan thanked her profusely and restored the claw to its place. Jules bought potions, then bid me farewell before heading to Dragon's Reach. I remained behind, no gold in my pockets but my bow at my side and Riverwood air in my lungs.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 368971.83, "x": 0.6463, "y": 0.5925, "ux": 0.1823, "uy": 0.6693}, {"id": 20, "actor": "Frodnar", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Riverwood, near the Wooden Door to Riverwood Trader, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Saw Faendal return to Riverwood with Jules the Breton. Overheard Camilla urging Jules to give Lucan the Golden Claw at the Riverwood Trader. Watched Jules leave toward the outskirts while Faendal made comments about Nord villages. Noted how strangers keep stirring up trouble near home.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 376581.69, "x": 0.7127, "y": 0.6364, "ux": 0.1972, "uy": 0.6555}, {"id": 21, "actor": "Embry", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Riverwood, near the Wooden Door to Riverwood Trader, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "See Faendal back in Riverwood with Jules, talking near the Riverwood Trader. Camilla Valerius gets excited about the Golden Claw, urging Jules to tell Lucan. Jules leaves for Dragon's Reach while Faendal stands by, smug about his archery. No one buys me a drink despite all the chatter.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 376581.69, "x": 0.6972, "y": 0.627, "ux": 0.1865, "uy": 0.6486}, {"id": 24, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Arcadia's Cauldron in Whiterun", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Buy a Potion of Cure Disease from Arcadia at Arcadia's Cauldron in Whiterun for 65 gold. Claimed to be infected with brown rot, though Arcadia questioned the diagnosis. She sold it anyway, noting I didn't look ill enough for such a disease.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 389009.58, "x": 0.7828, "y": 0.3366, "ux": 0.1533, "uy": 0.5745}, {"id": 25, "actor": "Nazeem", "emotion": "disgusted", "location": "Dragonsreach, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.6, "type": "RELATIONSHIP", "content": "Encountered Jules near Whiterun Stables, exchanged sharp words after she mocked my status. Later saw her in Dragonsreach speaking with Farengar Secret-Fire and Delphine, delivering the Dragonstone. Irileth summoned her when a dragon was sighted, and she left with the housecarl. Her sudden importance despite her commoner appearance is an affront to proper order.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 389009.58, "x": 0.6012, "y": 0.5398, "ux": 0.1867, "uy": 0.8266}, {"id": 26, "actor": "Irileth", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Dragonsreach and Western Watchtower Outskirts, Whiterun", "imp": 0.8, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Dragon sighted near Western Watchtower. Jarl Balgruuf ordered me to lead response; Farengar and Jules accompanied. Guard reported dragon circling but not attacking. Mustered men at main gate and dispatched to investigate wreckage for survivors and signs of further threat.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 399597.69, "x": 0.7662, "y": 0.3724, "ux": 0.1849, "uy": 0.8615}, {"id": 27, "actor": "Brenuin", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Close to Jorrvaskr, Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Nazeem sneers at Jules near Jorrvaskr, boasting about his farm and status. Carlotta and Olfina argue about rising produce costs and Stormcloak unrest nearby. Whiterun Guard marks the time of day with a casual remark. I observe from a distance, wary of the tension between the rich and struggling townsfolk.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 393121.62, "x": 0.6708, "y": 0.6086, "ux": 0.0629, "uy": 0.5828}, {"id": 28, "actor": "Unknown", "emotion": "annoyed", "location": "Belethor's General Goods in Whiterun", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Jules bought three Potions of Minor Stamina from Belethor for 195 gold at Belethor's General Goods in Whiterun. Belethor made a crude joke about selling relatives, laughing as usual. I stood nearby, arms crossed, irritated by the theatrics while firewood still needed delivering.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 393449.61, "x": 0.6757, "y": 0.5776, "ux": 0.1574, "uy": 0.57}, {"id": 29, "actor": "Carlotta Valentia", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Close to Jorrvaskr, Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Discussed rising produce costs with Olfina Gray-Mane near Jorrvaskr, blaming higher prices on war-related supply issues. Noted farmers are charging double, impacting my profit margins. Remained alert and focused while walking through the marketplace.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 393360.74, "x": 0.7127, "y": 0.3919, "ux": 0.054, "uy": 0.5691}, {"id": 30, "actor": "Fralia Gray-Mane", "emotion": "disgusted", "location": "Close to Jorrvaskr, Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Standing near Jorrvaskr, I called out my wares, promoting jewelry forged by Eorlund. Nazeem strutted past, boasting about his farm and sneering at travelers. His arrogance and Imperial sympathies soured the air, a reminder of the Battle-Borns' ilk. I turned my back on him, refusing to let his pride diminish my spirit.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 393360.74, "x": 0.7288, "y": 0.3352, "ux": 0.0596, "uy": 0.5903}, {"id": 31, "actor": "Unknown", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Close to Jorrvaskr, Whiterun", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Patrolled near Jorrvaskr as Ysolda and Carlotta discussed apples near Belethor's shop. Overheard Jon Battle-Born speaking with a Breton traveler named Jules about poetry and weapons. Later heard Carlotta complain about rising produce costs blamed on Stormcloak unrest. Kept watch as Fralia Gray-Mane hawked jewelry in the marketplace, her voice carrying over the crowd.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 393360.74, "x": 0.7256, "y": 0.4261, "ux": 0.0721, "uy": 0.5914}, {"id": 32, "actor": "Unknown", "emotion": "disgusted", "location": "Near Jorrvaskr, Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Observed Nazeem berating Jules near Jorrvaskr as she headed to the Cloud District. He mocked her poverty and boasted about his wealth from Chillfurrow Farm. Later, overheard Olfrid Battle-Born loudly asserting his clan's status nearby. No intervention needed—no laws broken, but the arrogance of both men was grating. Kept watch as Jules walked away without incident.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 396472.44, "x": 0.4661, "y": 0.7094, "ux": 0.0255, "uy": 0.567}, {"id": 33, "actor": "Jon Battle-Born", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Whiterun, near the Door to Belethor's General Goods, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Meet a well-armed Breton traveler near Belethor's shop in Whiterun. I comment on Skyrim's obsession with death; she responds with a sharp 'Well done.' I joke about preferring poetry to swords, recognizing her as the same traveler I've seen before—armed with a Nord greatsword and wearing Whiterun steel. Our exchange is brief but charged with mutual awareness, neither hostile nor familiar.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 393360.74, "x": 0.8993, "y": 0.3065, "ux": 0.2266, "uy": 0.6174}, {"id": 34, "actor": "Jarl Balgruuf the Greater", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Dragonsreach, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.9, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At Dragonsreach, I dispatched Irileth and Jules to investigate the Western Watchtower after a guard reported a dragon circling the area. Upon their return, Jules revealed she absorbed the dragon's power and may be Dragonborn, confirmed by the Greybeards' summons heard across the Reach. I granted her permission to purchase property in Whiterun and gave a gift from my armory for her prior service retrieving the Dragonstone. Farengar pressed for details on the dragon, but I prioritized Whiterun's safety over scholarly curiosity. Hrongar recognized the summons as a historic event, not seen since Tiber Septim.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 400494.26, "x": 0.7934, "y": 0.3326, "ux": 0.1979, "uy": 0.8539}, {"id": 35, "actor": "Whiterun Guard", "emotion": "traumatized", "location": "Western Watchtower Outskirts, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.9, "type": "TRAUMA", "content": "Fought Mirmulnir at the Western Watchtower Outskirts alongside Jules and Irileth. Charged the dragon shouting threats, took a fatal blow, and died moments before Jules felled the beast. Revived shortly after by unknown means, standing among the wreckage. Jules arrived an hour later, and I acknowledged her as the one who saved Whiterun that day.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 403410.55, "x": 0.7814, "y": 0.5796, "ux": 0.1716, "uy": 0.8319}, {"id": 36, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "surprised", "location": "Dragonsreach, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.9, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In Dragonsreach, I delivered the Dragonstone to Farengar Secret-Fire, who confirmed its significance. Delphine observed quietly before a guard reported a dragon sighting at the Western Watchtower. Jarl Balgruuf tasked me with joining Irileth to confront the dragon. At the watchtower, we fought Mirmulnir — I killed it, absorbed its soul, and learned I am Dragonborn. Back in Dragonsreach, the Jarl revealed the Greybeards summoned me, marking the beginning of a greater destiny.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 396472.44, "x": 0.75, "y": 0.1363, "ux": 0.2128, "uy": 0.8625}, {"id": 37, "actor": "Unknown", "emotion": "surprised", "location": "Close to Jorrvaskr, Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.8, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Saw Jules speak with Jon Battle-Born near Belethor's, then witnessed Nazeem sneer at her as she headed toward the Cloud District. Later, heard talk of a dragon being slain—confirmed it myself when I saw the body near the Western Watchtower. The Dragonborn legend lives. Whiterun may finally have hope.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 393360.74, "x": 0.7185, "y": 0.5544, "ux": 0.1649, "uy": 0.8567}, {"id": 38, "actor": "Lillith Maiden-Loom", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Whiterun Stables, near the Door to Whiterun, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Received 44 gold from Skulvar at Whiterun Stables after reviewing weekly earnings. Discussed increased horse rental demand due to war traffic. Observed Jules near Jorrvaskr, armed and purposeful, possibly needing stable services. Overheard Nazeem boasting about Chillfurrow Farm while Olfrid Battle-Born and Olfina Gray-Mane exchanged heated words about clan loyalties.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 391201.02, "x": 0.7189, "y": 0.5055, "ux": 0.1123, "uy": 0.5958}, {"id": 39, "actor": "Irileth", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Western Watchtower Outskirts, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.9, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought Mirmulnir the dragon at Western Watchtower with Whiterun Guards and Jules. All guards except one died in the battle; killed the dragon after prolonged combat. Reported to Jarl Balgruuf in Dragonsreach, where Jules was named Thane and Dragonborn. Remain wary of further dragon threats to Whiterun.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 406852.95, "x": 0.8186, "y": 0.4782, "ux": 0.1781, "uy": 0.8495}, {"id": 40, "actor": "Farengar Secret-Fire", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Dragonsreach in Whiterun", "imp": 0.9, "type": "KNOWLEDGE", "content": "In Dragonsreach, I questioned the adventurer who retrieved the Dragonstone from Bleak Falls Barrow, confirming its arrival. Delphine, my mysterious collaborator, verified the find and pressed for swift analysis. When Irileth reported a dragon sighted near the Western Watchtower, I urged immediate study, but Balgruuf ordered Irileth and the adventurer to investigate while I remained to research defenses. Later, the adventurer described the dragon using a Thu'um—a confirmed, terrifying use of the Voice—validating ancient texts and deepening the urgency of my work.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 397642.32, "x": 0.7823, "y": 0.1232, "ux": 0.2405, "uy": 0.8599}, {"id": 41, "actor": "Anoriath", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Close to Jorrvaskr, Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Overheard Jules exchange words with Jon Battle-Born near Belethor's General Goods, then later watched her brush off Nazeem's mockery near Jorrvaskr. Nazeem bragged about owning Chillfurrow Farm while looking down on her, but she remained unfazed. Heard Carlotta and Olfina discuss rising produce costs tied to Stormcloak unrest. Walked past Fralia Gray-Mane hawking jewelry near Jorrvaskr, with Ysolda complimenting her wares.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 393360.74, "x": 0.6461, "y": 0.5618, "ux": 0.0576, "uy": 0.5897}, {"id": 42, "actor": "Olfina Gray-Mane", "emotion": "content", "location": "Close to Jorrvaskr, Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Overheard Nazeem sneering at Jules near Jorrvaskr, boasting about his farm and mocking her status. Later, spoke with Carlotta Valentia outside the Bannered Mare about rising produce costs blamed on Stormcloak unrest. Reminded her the Gray-Manes stand with true Nords, not Empire-sympathizing elites like Nazeem. Felt satisfaction defending our cause while upholding family honor.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 396472.44, "x": 0.5934, "y": 0.5913, "ux": 0.0492, "uy": 0.5692}, {"id": 43, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "content", "location": "Sleeping Giant Inn, Hold: Riverwood", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Woke up at the Sleeping Giant Inn in Riverwood after a full night's rest, feeling refreshed and ready to continue my journey to Solitude. Spoke with Orgnar about available food and drink, then purchased cabbage soup, cooked pogfish, and eidar cheese for 43 gold. Overheard Sven performing Imperial loyalist ballads while Delphine expressed frustration over delayed shipments from Whiterun. Lydia noted the supply issue might involve bandits or negligence, suggesting an investigation.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 416561.56, "x": 0.6955, "y": 0.2422, "ux": 0.2873, "uy": 0.9689}, {"id": 44, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Sleeping Giant Inn, Hold: Riverwood", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Walking through the Sleeping Giant Inn in Riverwood, I observe Delphine questioning Jules about their presence. Orgnar serves food and drink with his usual gruff efficiency. Sven performs songs favoring the Imperials, drawing murmurs from patrons. I comment to Delphine that delayed shipments from Whiterun could be due to bandits or negligence — someone should investigate. Later, at Lucan's Dry Goods, I note the unusually high coin in Lucan’s possession after Jules returns from dealing with thieves.", "day": "21st of Last Seed", "gt": 417222.06, "x": 0.5514, "y": 0.486, "ux": 0.2843, "uy": 0.9736}, {"id": 47, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Dragonsreach, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At Dragonsreach, Jules sold Dragon Bile and Dragon Rheum to Farengar Secret-Fire for 400 gold and purchased potions and spells. Faendal commented on the transaction but raised no objections. We are now preparing to travel to Riften.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 463490.46, "x": 0.5946, "y": 0.3933, "ux": 0.1605, "uy": 0.7681}, {"id": 48, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Dragonsreach, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In Dragonsreach, Farengar Secret-Fire buys Dragon Bile and Dragon Rheum from Jules for 400 gold total. Jules purchases a Spell Tome: Candlelight and a Spell Tome: Healing, spending 282 gold. I remark that Farengar's coin is as good as any, though I distrust his experiments.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 470034.34, "x": 0.5173, "y": 0.4004, "ux": 0.1619, "uy": 0.776}, {"id": 49, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "content", "location": "Dragonsreach, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Sell dragon bile and dragon rheum to Farengar Secret-Fire at Dragonsreach for 400 gold total. Purchased spell tomes of Candlelight and Healing, spending 282 gold. Farengar suggested joining the Mages College in Winterhold. Lydia and Faendal accompanied me; Faendal remarked on my newfound coin.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 470034.34, "x": 0.693, "y": 0.091, "ux": 0.1602, "uy": 0.7781}, {"id": 50, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Belethor's General Goods in Whiterun", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Traded supplies with Belethor at his shop in Whiterun while Lydia stood guard. Lydia exchanged sharp words with Belethor, expressing distrust. Jules completed the transaction without incident. We left promptly for Riften.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 473616.11, "x": 0.9277, "y": 0.4049, "ux": 0.3064, "uy": 0.6866}, {"id": 51, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Whiterun, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In Whiterun, Jules challenged Nazeem to a duel. Before Nazeem could properly respond, Faendal suddenly killed him. I kept my hand on my sword, watching closely, then affirmed to Faendal that Nazeem had brought it upon himself with his arrogance.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 481090.51, "x": 0.6546, "y": 0.78, "ux": 0.0, "uy": 0.5468}, {"id": 52, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "White River Watch, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At White River Watch, Lydia and Faendal fought beside me as I killed a wolf attacking us. Lydia coordinated our defense, keeping watch on my flank while I brought the beast down with my greatsword. Later, a madwoman spoke of a missing master and someone named Dervenin near Solitude, warning me the armor I wear won't help find him. I offered to look for him when I reach Solitude.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 481227.54, "x": 0.9919, "y": 0.2211, "ux": 0.3405, "uy": 0.6545}, {"id": 53, "actor": "Commander Caius", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Close to Jorrvaskr, Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Walking near Jorrvaskr in Whiterun, I observed Jules trading with Anoriath at the market. She purchased large quantities of garlic and salt pile for 84 gold—unusual for a traveler, suggesting long-term provisioning. Overheard Faendal in Dragonsreach earlier mentioning Jules dealing in dragon parts with Farengar, raising suspicion about her activities and connections.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 472379.04, "x": 0.5957, "y": 0.6211, "ux": 0.1514, "uy": 0.56}, {"id": 54, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "content", "location": "Whiterun, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.75, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Killed Nazeem in the streets of Whiterun after Jules challenged him to a duel. My dagger ended him when he refused to back down, with Lydia watching closely. She acknowledged the kill was just, though I care little for Nord approval. Still no coin from Jules, and my name was mangled again—'FanDoll' this time—but the blade speaks clearer than words.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 478035.96, "x": 0.7569, "y": 0.7465, "ux": 0.0059, "uy": 0.5446}, {"id": 55, "actor": "Amren", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Close to Jorrvaskr, Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.6, "type": "RELATIONSHIP", "content": "Walking near Jorrvaskr, I overhear Braith bullying Lars Battle-Born again, demanding his money. Saffir confronts me about my mercenary work, insisting we can't afford my obsession with recovering my father's sword. Later, I see Jules trade with Anoriath, buying garlic and salt, while Carlotta calls out her produce nearby. The tension between my duty as a father and my honor as a Redguard weighs heavily.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 468954.48, "x": 0.4881, "y": 0.5456, "ux": 0.3434, "uy": 0.3732}, {"id": 56, "actor": "Mila Valentia", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Close to Jorrvaskr, Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Standing near Jorrvaskr, I watch Anoriath sell fresh meat to the Breton woman, Jules, who buys garlic, salt, and several types of meat. My mother Carlotta calls out nearby, selling vegetables as usual. I hear Nazeem shout angrily later, then Lydia warns him sharply, hand on her sword. Faendal comments dryly after the tension fades, and I think how brave Lydia looks protecting Whiterun.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 474541.11, "x": 0.8729, "y": 0.4138, "ux": 0.1303, "uy": 0.5361}, {"id": 57, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "reflective", "location": "Near The Ritual Stone, The Ritual Doomstone, Outdoors, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.85, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Diary Entry: Another day threaded with blood and strange omens. I write this by the dim glow of my *Candlelight* spell, the Ritual Stone looming like a rotten tooth in the gray afternoon. My arms still hum from the greatsword’s weight — not just from the wolf at White River Watch, but from the weight of what’s pressing in.\n\nThat fight was clean, at least. Lydia’s voice cutting through the snarls: *“Jules, right flank!”* — and me pivoting, steel meeting fang, the wet crunch of bone under frost-tempered iron. I felt the impact shiver up my arms, the heat of exertion blooming beneath my armor. Faendal’s arrow took the second beast before it even broke cover. Efficient. Necessary. But it’s the madwoman’s words that cling like burrs, not the wolf’s blood.\n\nShe spoke of a master lost, of Dervenin, of Solitude. Said my armor wouldn’t help me find him. As if she saw through me — through the steel and spells, straight to the girl from the Heartland chasing a grandmother’s dream. I offered to look, of course. What else does a bard’s heir do but listen to stories, even the fractured ones?\n\nAnd the Jarl’s summons — Mirmulnir, the soul tearing into me like a winter gale, the Word on my tongue before I knew I spoke it. *Dragonborn.* Still feels like a borrowed title, too large for my shoulders. Yet the gold from Farengar for the bile and rheum is real enough — 400 septims clinking in my belt pouch, 282 spent on *Healing* and *Candlelight*. Practical magic, the kind Nana would’ve scoffed at. She sang wounds closed, not cast them. Farengar suggested Winterhold. I almost laughed. Me? Among the robe-swirlers and scrying pools? But the thought lingers. Magic is power, and power keeps me alive between here and Solitude.\n\nFaendal watches the trees, bow loose in his hands. Lydia stands like a statue, scanning the ridgeline. They’ve both seen me fight, seen the dragon’s soul burn in my eyes. Do they see a warrior? A curiosity? Or just another blade for hire? I killed Nazeem’s words with steel this morning — a petty thing, perhaps, but satisfying. Still, it’s the madwoman’s warning that echoes: *Don’t go to the Blue Palace. Don’t listen to Dervenin.*\n\nI’ll go to Solitude. I’ll find the Bard’s College. And if Dervenin stands in the way, or the Blue Palace hides traps, then let them come. Nana’s songs are in my blood, and now, something older. I’ll sing my way through if I must — or shout a Word that tears the sky.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 447584.24, "x": 0.8222, "y": 0.1547, "ux": 0.2942, "uy": 0.7522}, {"id": 58, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Near The Ritual Stone, The Ritual Doomstone, Outdoors, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At The Ritual Stone in Whiterun, Lydia and Faendal fought off a pair of attacking wolves—Faendal felled one with an arrow, Lydia struck down the other. Faendal kept his bow ready, calm and watchful, while Lydia coordinated our defense. I confirmed he still had his bow, and we pressed forward, alert for more threats. The madwoman’s words about Dervenin and the Blue Palace echo in my mind.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 487989.07, "x": 0.9266, "y": 0.126, "ux": 0.3278, "uy": 0.6768}, {"id": 59, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Skyrim Wilderness, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought alongside Faendal and Jules near The Ritual Stone, killing multiple wolves threatening the group. Coordinated tactics with Faendal, covering his shot while he took down a doe by the ridge. Later killed a mudcrab at a waterside in the wilderness. Maintained defensive stance throughout, shield raised and sword ready.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 487989.07, "x": 0.6151, "y": 0.502, "ux": 0.3091, "uy": 0.5579}, {"id": 60, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Skyrim Wilderness, Outdoors", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Hunted deer near The Ritual Stone with Jules and Lydia. Dropped a doe at Lydia's call while Jules repeatedly mispronounced my name. Continued hunting despite growing irritation at being disrespected. Maintained focus on archery and situational awareness.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 489256.76, "x": 0.7403, "y": 0.5488, "ux": 0.3586, "uy": 0.6153}, {"id": 61, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "content", "location": "Valtheim Towers, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "We cleared Valtheim Towers of bandits — I personally killed a Bandit Outlaw, two regular bandits, and the Bandit Chief, taking point on the stairs while Faendal covered the door with his bow. The fight was sharp; one bandit tried to submit after I'd already broken through their line, but I finished it. Tower secured, Jules settled in to read through a stack of books she found inside while Faendal and I coordinated watch positions — him near the door for angles on the outside, me holding the stairs against anything rising from below. We're bedding down here for the night.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 497343.45, "x": 0.7799, "y": 0.4625, "ux": 0.3476, "uy": 0.7281}, {"id": 62, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "content", "location": "Valtheim Towers, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.65, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Traveled from the Ritual Stone toward Valtheim Towers with Lydia and Faendal, fighting off multiple wolves, mudcrabs, and a slaughterfish along the way — Faendal handled most with his bow while Lydia and I took what closed in. We pushed into Valtheim Towers itself to shelter for the night and found it held by a bandit gang; I killed one bandit, Lydia cut down the bandit chief, the bandit outlaw, and two more, while Faendal covered from range. After the fight I settled in and read several books from the bandits' shelves — The Song of Pelinal volumes, Mysterious Akavir, A Dance in Fire, Mystery of Talara, and Life of Uriel Septim VII. Lydia called the tower clear around 8 PM and told me to rest; Faendal took position near the door, Lydia held the stairs.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 490747.37, "x": 0.8864, "y": 0.1773, "ux": 0.3188, "uy": 0.7329}, {"id": 63, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Valtheim Towers, Whiterun Hold, Outdoors", "imp": 0.75, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Spent the night at Valtheim Towers reading The Black Arrow Vol. 2 before sleeping. Woke at dawn to Lydia and Faendal debating Nord versus Bosmer tracking methods — Faendal argued Bosmer read what the forest is *about* to do, Lydia countered that steel beats instinct when something's already on you. Vignar Gray-Mane arrived at the tower bearing a message from Irileth: Ulfric has declared war on the Thalmor, Whiterun sits between hammers, and Jarl Balgruuf needs capable allies close at hand. I told Vignar to relay to Balgruuf that I'm heading to the Greybeards as instructed — he acknowledged it and departed for Dragonsreach. Now moving with Lydia and Faendal toward High Hrothgar, wary of increased Thalmor Justiciar patrols on the mountain roads.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 504778.05, "x": 0.8935, "y": 0.2496, "ux": 0.3024, "uy": 0.7428}, {"id": 64, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Valtheim Towers, Whiterun Hold, Outdoors", "imp": 0.72, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Vignar Gray-Mane rode out to Valtheim Towers personally with a message from Irileth: the Stormcloaks have declared war on the Thalmor, and Whiterun is caught between hammers — the Jarl wants capable allies close at hand. Jules told him to relay to Balgruuf that she's heading to the Greybeards as he instructed, and Vignar departed for Dragonsreach. Earlier that morning I'd had a proper exchange with Faendal about Bosmer tracking — he reads what the forest is *about* to do rather than what it's already done; I respect the craft even if I'd still back steel once blades are drawn. We broke camp and moved out, Faendal noting aloud that Justiciar patrols between here and High Hrothgar will be thicker and more dangerous now, and he's right — we keep moving and stay alert.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 504628.67, "x": 0.8718, "y": 0.3859, "ux": 0.2803, "uy": 0.7462}, {"id": 65, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Valtheim Towers, Whiterun Hold, then road near Darkshade", "imp": 0.72, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Spent the night at Valtheim Towers after clearing it with Jules and Lydia. At dawn, Lydia asked me about Bosmer tracking methods — a genuine question, not mockery — and I explained how we read the forest ahead of the moment rather than the signs it leaves behind. She pushed back in favor of steel over instinct, but the exchange was honest. Vignar Gray-Mane arrived with a message from Irileth: Ulfric has declared war on the Thalmor, Whiterun sits between hammers, and the Jarl wants capable allies close. I told Vignar plainly that Stormcloaks and Thalmor bleeding each other troubles me little, but Whiterun caught between them is a different problem. Now we're moving toward Darkshade en route to the Greybeards, and I've noted aloud that Justiciar patrols will be thicker on these roads — and they'll see a Bosmer elf with Nords and draw their own dangerous conclusions.", "day": "22nd of Last Seed", "gt": 502707.53, "x": 0.8685, "y": 0.3341, "ux": 0.2754, "uy": 0.7165}, {"id": 66, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Skyrim Wilderness, Outdoors, near Darkwater Crossing, Eastmarch", "imp": 0.45, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Traveling east through Eastmarch toward Ivarstead, we collectively decided to skip the direct route through Windhelm and Riften given the new Stormcloak-Thalmor war — too much risk of armed patrols demanding explanations. Near Lost Knife Hideout, I killed a wolf on reflex and felt immediate guilt — that animal didn't deserve it, just a creature in the wrong place. Wolves attacked again later in the Skyrim wilderness; I cut one down while a Dark Elf Vigilant of Stendarr finished the other. The Vigilant warned me sternly against daedric dealings before we moved on — Faendal noted dryly he'd rather deal with Daedra hunters than Justiciars, though not linger long enough for them to start scrutinizing him. We bypassed Hillgrund's Tomb without entering and are now pressing toward Ivarstead, the whole party tense after Ulfric's declaration of war.", "day": "23rd of Last Seed", "gt": 549926.71, "x": 0.7573, "y": 0.3207, "ux": 0.3278, "uy": 0.5684}, {"id": 67, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Skyrim Wilderness, Eastmarch, Outdoors", "imp": 0.35, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Traveling with Jules and Lydia through Eastmarch toward Ivarstead, we skirted Hillgrund's Tomb and agreed to take the direct road — fewer chances to run into Stormcloak or Thalmor patrols. A wolf attacked on the road; Jules put it down. Farther along, we encountered Vigilants of Stendarr in the wilderness — one threatened Jules over Daedra dealings. I kept my distance, wary of a Dunmer Vigilant asking why an elf is traveling armed in this company, and we moved on without incident.", "day": "23rd of Last Seed", "gt": 549926.71, "x": 0.6773, "y": 0.5859, "ux": 0.3024, "uy": 0.5532}, {"id": 68, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Skyrim Wilderness, Outdoors, east of Lost Knife Hideout toward Darkwater Crossing", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Traveling east toward Ivarstead with Jules and Faendal, moving through Eastmarch to avoid Windhelm while Stormcloaks and Thalmor Justiciars are clashing near Kynesgrove — keeping clear of that mess is plain sense. Jules killed a wolf that hit us on the road; no injuries to the group. Further along, we spotted movement in the trees — Vigilants of Stendarr, not Justiciars, watching the road and warning Jules against Daedra dealings. Faendal was right to move us past them quickly — no point giving Daedra hunters time to ask about the elf in our company.", "day": "23rd of Last Seed", "gt": 549926.71, "x": 0.6392, "y": 0.5406, "ux": 0.3131, "uy": 0.5431}, {"id": 69, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Some distance from Sarethi Farm, The Rift, Skyrim, Outdoors", "imp": 0.38, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Traveling through Eastmarch and into The Rift on Loredas, the party fought through two wolf attacks — Faendal and Lydia coordinated well, and I killed the second wolf myself. Near the Rift Stormcloak Camp, I cut down a skeever barely worth the effort. A Dunmer thief ambushed us near Sarethi Farm, demanded valuables, and when I dismissed him outright, Lydia ran him down and killed him. We passed Sarethi Farm — overheard the young farmhand Aduri muttering about her boring life — then spotted Ivarstead across the water with the Seven Thousand Steps looming beyond it.", "day": "23rd of Last Seed", "gt": 558687.99, "x": 0.8559, "y": 0.2222, "ux": 0.3317, "uy": 0.5891}, {"id": 70, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "content", "location": "Skyrim Wilderness, Eastmarch into The Rift, near Sarethi Farm and Ivarstead", "imp": 0.42, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Traveled through Eastmarch and into The Rift toward Ivarstead on Loredas, fighting two wolves and a skeever — Jules killed them all — plus a Dunmer thief who tried to rob us near Sarethi Farm and got cut down by Lydia for his trouble. Lydia asked me about Bosmer afterlife beliefs mid-march; I told her we go back to the Hunting Grounds, not Sovngarde — she took it in stride, which I appreciate more than I expected. We passed Sarethi Farm outskirts, briefly heard a young Dunmer farmhand complaining about her dull life, and finally spotted Ivarstead across the water. The road was bloodier than I'd like for a Loredas, but we're intact and the Seven Thousand Steps are nearly in reach.", "day": "23rd of Last Seed", "gt": 558775.09, "x": 0.7696, "y": 0.3109, "ux": 0.3294, "uy": 0.5795}, {"id": 71, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "content", "location": "Some distance from Sarethi Farm, The Rift, Skyrim, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Traveled the road from near Darkwater Crossing toward Ivarstead on Loredas with Jules and Faendal, fighting off wolves along the way — Jules took one down cleanly while Faendal and I coordinated shots and held the line. Near the Rift Stormcloak Camp, Jules killed a skeever without breaking stride. Close to Sarethi Farm, a Dunmer thief tried to rob Jules at knifepoint; when Jules dismissed him and walked away, he charged — I cut him down. After the fight Jules thanked me, and I told her no thanks were needed, though I won't pretend my feet aren't earning their keep today. Left Jules on watch at Sarethi Farm Outskirts while Faendal and I discussed Bosmer afterlife beliefs; Ivarstead is now in sight.", "day": "23rd of Last Seed", "gt": 558775.09, "x": 0.5151, "y": 0.7069, "ux": 0.3012, "uy": 0.5401}, {"id": 75, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "content", "location": "Vilemyr Inn, Ivarstead", "imp": 0.55, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At Vilemyr Inn in Ivarstead, Lynly Star-Sung played a lute song about lost love and the northern stars. Faendal and Lydia listened quietly as I sat refreshed from sleep, the weight of the dragon and war briefly forgotten. The music brought a rare peace to our company.", "day": "23rd of Last Seed", "gt": 575921.26, "x": 0.7807, "y": 0.1581, "ux": 0.1776, "uy": 0.4063}, {"id": 76, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "content", "location": "Skyrim Wilderness, Outdoors", "imp": 0.7, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought and killed a troll in the Skyrim wilderness alongside Jules and Faendal. Jules used the 'Fus' shout to stagger it, Faendal landed a clean neck shot, and I finished it with my axe. Afterward, Karita warned us of wolves on the path to High Hrothgar. We pressed on, vigilant and ready for more threats.", "day": "23rd of Last Seed", "gt": 575921.26, "x": 0.6347, "y": 0.5981, "ux": 0.3144, "uy": 0.5521}, {"id": 77, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Vilemyr Inn to High Hrothgar, Hold: The Rift and Whiterun", "imp": 0.78, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Walking with Jules and Lydia from Vilemyr Inn toward High Hrothgar after Jules woke from sleep. Exchanged words with Lydia about M'aiq and mispronunciations, a subtle jab at how she — and others — butcher names without thought. Killed a troll in the wilds; my arrow took it through the neck, Lydia commended the shot. No coin still from Jules for past kills, and 'Fandol' stings like the others — another slight in a journey growing thin on trust.", "day": "23rd of Last Seed", "gt": 575921.26, "x": 0.615, "y": 0.6435, "ux": 0.3496, "uy": 0.6335}, {"id": 93, "actor": "Arngeir", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "High Hrothgar, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.8, "type": "SKILL", "content": "Jules, the Breton Dragonborn, arrived at High Hrothgar after answering the summons. I tested her Voice — she shouted 'Fus' and then learned 'Ro' from Master Einarth. She demonstrated Unrelenting Force in the courtyard under Borri's guidance. Lydia and Faendal observed, offering terse commentary on her progress and my teachings.", "day": "23rd of Last Seed", "gt": 599927.34, "x": 0.6413, "y": 0.4408, "ux": 0.3556, "uy": 0.8322}, {"id": 94, "actor": "Wulfgar", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "High Hrothgar, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.85, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Jules, the Dragonborn, demonstrates Unrelenting Force at High Hrothgar under Arngeir's guidance. I observe as she learns 'Ro' from Einarth and practices the Shout with Borri's assistance. Her Voice is raw but true, carrying the blood of dragons. The mountain feels the resonance of a destined one awakening.", "day": "23rd of Last Seed", "gt": 599927.34, "x": 0.6702, "y": 0.4128, "ux": 0.3538, "uy": 0.8233}, {"id": 95, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "content", "location": "High Hrothgar, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.85, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Standing in High Hrothgar's courtyard, I watch Jules learn 'Ro' from Master Einarth under Arngeir's guidance. Her shout—Fus Ro—strikes the target with precision, earning praise from the Greybeards. I feel a surge of pride despite Arngeir's warning that the trial isn't mine to share. The weight of our oath deepens as the mountain echoes with the Voice of the Dragonborn.", "day": "23rd of Last Seed", "gt": 599927.34, "x": 0.7411, "y": 0.3256, "ux": 0.3505, "uy": 0.8019}, {"id": 96, "actor": "Einarth", "emotion": "content", "location": "High Hrothgar in Whiterun", "imp": 0.8, "type": "SKILL", "content": "Taught Jules the Word of Power 'Ro' (Balance) at High Hrothgar, transferring my understanding of the second word of Unrelenting Force. Observed her rapid mastery during target practice under Arngeir's guidance. Though bound by silence, I affirmed her potential as Dragonborn. The mountain listens — and answers.", "day": "23rd of Last Seed", "gt": 599927.34, "x": 0.671, "y": 0.4784, "ux": 0.3632, "uy": 0.816}, {"id": 97, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "surprised", "location": "High Hrothgar, Whiterun", "imp": 0.85, "type": "SKILL", "content": "At High Hrothgar, Master Arngeir tested my Voice after I climbed the Seven Thousand Steps. I shouted 'Fus Ro' and staggered him, proving my Dragonborn nature. Einarth taught me the Word of Power 'Ro'—'Balance'—and I practiced Unrelenting Force under Borri's guidance. Lydia watched, tense but proud, as I struck practice targets with growing precision. Arngeir acknowledged my promise, warning the true path is long and shaped by breath, not steel.", "day": "23rd of Last Seed", "gt": 599927.34, "x": 0.8186, "y": 0.2039, "ux": 0.3571, "uy": 0.8038}, {"id": 98, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "High Hrothgar, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.75, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Standing in High Hrothgar's hall, I watch Jules absorb the Word of Power 'Ro' from Master Einarth as Arngeir instructs. The air thrums when she combines Fus and Ro, striking the target with precision that impresses even the Greybeards. Lydia stands guard, visibly awed despite herself, while I remain silent near the bench—unseen, unpaid, and still called 'Fiend' by Jules. The monks speak of destiny, but I wonder how much of it is earned and how much is simply surviving the fools you travel with.", "day": "23rd of Last Seed", "gt": 599927.34, "x": 0.6364, "y": 0.4608, "ux": 0.3672, "uy": 0.7489}, {"id": 99, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "angry", "location": "High Hrothgar, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.8, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Standing outside High Hrothgar, I told Jules 'home' was not a word I needed reminded of, not after fighting trolls, clearing tombs, and giving her my arrows without coin or thanks. Lydia spoke up for me, calling it 'sharp' to dismiss me so — the only one with honor enough to see it. I stayed long enough to see Borri teach the Word 'Wuld', then turned toward Riverwood, boots crunching snow, heart colder than the wind off the mountain.", "day": "24th of Last Seed", "gt": 606459.69, "x": 0.6772, "y": 0.4593, "ux": 0.3544, "uy": 0.7644}, {"id": 100, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "High Hrothgar, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.85, "type": "SKILL", "content": "At High Hrothgar, Master Borri taught me the Word of Power 'Wuld'—Whirlwind—after Faendal departed. I mastered Whirlwind Sprint quickly, impressing Arngeir, who then tasked me with retrieving Jurgen Windcaller's Horn from Ustengrav. Lydia reaffirmed her loyalty as we prepared to leave, despite dangers ahead. Arngeir and Wulfgar spoke in low tones, concerned about what might await me in the tomb.", "day": "24th of Last Seed", "gt": 606459.69, "x": 0.8638, "y": 0.2054, "ux": 0.3782, "uy": 0.7703}, {"id": 101, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "High Hrothgar, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.85, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At High Hrothgar, I watched Jules learn the 'Wuld' shout from Master Borri under Arngeir's guidance. She mastered Whirlwind Sprint swiftly after Wulfgar demonstrated it, impressing the Greybeards. When Jules was given the final trial—retrieving Jurgen Windcaller's horn from Ustengrav—I affirmed to Wulfgar that I would stand at her back, no matter what awaited in the tomb. Faendal departed for Riverwood after being dismissed, having served loyally since Whiterun.", "day": "24th of Last Seed", "gt": 606459.69, "x": 0.7121, "y": 0.4731, "ux": 0.3755, "uy": 0.772}, {"id": 102, "actor": "Unknown", "emotion": "", "location": "", "imp": 0.7, "type": "KNOWLEDGE", "content": "Jules killed Nazeem. In broad daylight. She challenged him to a fair duel, and he accepted, then Jules struck Nazeem down in a single blow with her greatsword. No struggle. Instant obliteration.", "day": null, "gt": 0, "x": 0.4181, "y": 1.0, "ux": 0.0089, "uy": 0.5322}, {"id": 105, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "content", "location": "Pinepeak Cavern Outskirts, Hold: The Rift, Outdoors", "imp": 0.55, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At Pinepeak Cavern outskirts in The Rift, I fought alongside Jules and Lydia against a male bear. My arrows helped bring it down, though Jules delivered the killing blow. Lydia called out tactics during the fight, and I acknowledged her form—remarking on Riverwood afterward as we moved toward Ivarstead. No coin exchanged, and my name was misheard again, but the hunt was clean.", "day": "24th of Last Seed", "gt": 623649.66, "x": 0.8303, "y": 0.4845, "ux": 0.3092, "uy": 0.6181}, {"id": 106, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "content", "location": "Vilemyr Inn, Hold: Ivarstead", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought and killed two bears near Pinepeak Cavern—one outside, one inside—with Jules and Faendal. Cleared the cave, found a book on heavy armor forging that Jules read. Slept at Vilemyr Inn in Ivarstead, woke to town talk of wolves, bears, and haunted barrows. Temba Wide-Arm complained about bear damage to timber, while Wilhelm warned of Shroud Hearth Barrow's ghosts.", "day": "24th of Last Seed", "gt": 628814.41, "x": 0.6868, "y": 0.4683, "ux": 0.288, "uy": 0.5729}, {"id": 107, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "content", "location": "Vilemyr Inn in Ivarstead", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Woke up at Vilemyr Inn in Ivarstead after a deep, restful sleep. Spoke with Wilhelm, bought hot beef stew and travel packs for 196 gold. Overheard Barknar warn of wolves and Temba complain about bear-damaged timber. The guard mentioned the Dragonborn summoning, confirming the weight of my path forward.", "day": "24th of Last Seed", "gt": 628814.41, "x": 0.7155, "y": 0.2214, "ux": 0.3193, "uy": 0.8315}, {"id": 108, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "content", "location": "Ivarstead (Waterside), Hold: The Rift, Outdoors", "imp": 0.45, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Diary Entry: Slept like the dead last night, and Mara bless it, I needed that. Told Lydia this morning I felt like I could've slept through a dragon crashing through the roof — she just grunted something about earned rest and told me to eat my bread. Fair enough. After the Seven Thousand Steps down from High Hrothgar, my legs had opinions about ever climbing anything again.\n\nIvarstead in the morning light is a sleepy little thing. Bought stew and a couple of travel packs off Wilhelm before we left the inn — 196 gold, which stings a bit less now that Farengar's coin is still padding my purse. Overheard the guard outside grumbling about wanting his furs, and Barknar warning some poor soul about wolves on the mountain path while Temba complained louder about bears wrecking her timber stock. Small-town troubles. Almost quaint, after everything.\n\nBut it was the guard's other words that snagged me — *the Greybeards have summoned the Dragonborn to High Hrothgar, hasn't happened in hundreds of years.* Said so plainly, like weather. Like I wasn't standing three feet away with the Horn of Jurgen Windcaller sitting unclaimed somewhere in Ustengrav, waiting on me to go dig it out of whatever's guarding it. Strange, hearing your own myth spoken aloud by a stranger who has no idea you're the punchline.\n\nI keep turning over what happened at High Hrothgar, honestly — feels like it hasn't finished settling in me yet. Borri teaching me *Wuld*, the Word of Whirlwind, and it just... clicking, like a verse I already knew the tune to. Arngeir's face when I mastered it so fast — that mix of astonishment and worry he tries to keep off his face and mostly fails at. He's not subtle, for a man who's spent decades cultivating silence. And then the warning, him and Wulfgar murmuring together like they didn't want me to hear, about what might be waiting in that tomb. I heard enough. Enough to know it isn't nothing.\n\nLydia reaffirmed she's coming with me regardless — didn't even hesitate when I brought up maybe splitting the risk. Just gave me that flat, unimpressed housecarl look, the one that says *don't insult me by suggesting it again.* I won't lie, there's a comfort in that steadiness. Nana used to say a bard is only as good as the people who'll stand at the edge of the firelight while she sings — meaning, I think, that stories need witnesses, need someone keeping watch so the teller can lose herself in the telling. Lydia's that, in her own way. Faendal too, when he's near, though he's drifted looser these past days, more habit than oath.\n\nWalking down through Ivarstead's cobbled bridge this morning, the leaves doing that gorgeous burnt-orange thing they do this time of year, I let myself just... breathe for a minute. Didn't think about Ustengrav, or the horn, or Dragonborn, or war. Just the sound of water under stone and Lydia's boots on the path beside me. Small mercies. The kind Nana would've called a verse worth remembering even if it never makes it into the song.\n\nBecause the song's coming, isn't it. Ulfric's declared war on the Thalmor now — actual war, not just growling across a table. Word reached even sleepy little Ivarstead: clashes near Kynesgrove, routing at Windhelm's gates. The whole east side of Skyrim is a tinderbox and I keep threading through it like I've got all the time in the world, chasing horns and Words of Power while armies gather. There's a tension in that I try not to look at too directly — like a wound you know is there but don't want to prod. Best to keep moving, keep the road ahead sharper in my mind than the road behind.\n\nStill mulling on the madwoman's warning too, if I'm honest — Dervenin, the Blue Palace, all that. Haven't forgotten it, just... shelved it, the way you shelve a story you're not ready to tell yet. Solitude's still out there, still waiting, still holding the Bard's College and whatever answers that woman was pointing me toward. But Ustengrav comes first. Arngeir was clear enough about that, and much as I chafe sometimes at being *directed*, I understand the shape of it — prove myself with the horn, then maybe the rest of the path opens up.\n\nWe're pressing out from Ivarstead again shortly, back toward the mountain road and whatever waits past it. My arms have mostly stopped aching from that wolf fight at White River Watch, though my mind hasn't quite let go of Mirmulnir's soul tearing into me, or the weight of that first true Shout. Two Words mastered now — *Fus Ro* and *Wuld* — and each one feels less like something I learned and more like something I *remembered*, which is a stranger thought than I like sitting with for too long.\n\nFor now, though: stew in my belly, boots on solid ground, Lydia at my shoulder scanning the treeline like she always does. Ustengrav waits. Whatever's guarding that horn, I'll meet it with steel in hand and a Word ready on my tongue if it comes to that. Nana always said the best stories have teeth. Guess I'm about to find out if mine do too.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 716357.51, "x": 0.8237, "y": 0.1864, "ux": 0.3143, "uy": 0.7674}, {"id": 109, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "reflective", "location": "Ivarstead (Waterside), Hold: The Rift, Outdoors", "imp": 0.65, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Diary Entry: Morning in Ivarstead, and my legs have finally stopped aching from that mountain. Small mercies. I'm sitting near the water listening to it run under the bridge, waiting on Jules to finish whatever business she's got with the guards, and I find myself wanting to put down what's happened these past few days before it all blurs together the way hard marches tend to do.\n\nHigh Hrothgar. Gods, I still feel the cold of that place in my knees. I stood in that courtyard and watched Jules — my Thane, a woman I was still half-sizing up not two moons past — pull the Voice itself out of the air like she was born to it. Fus Ro, clean as a blade strike, and the Greybeards nodding like she'd passed some test they didn't expect her to pass so quick. Then Wuld, and she was just *gone*, a blur across the stones and back again before I'd finished blinking. I've fought beside shieldmaidens who trained their whole lives for half that grace. It isn't training. It's something else entirely, and I won't pretend it doesn't put a chill in me that has nothing to do with mountain air.\n\nAnd then they gave her the real task. Not words this time — an object. A horn, sitting in some tomb called Ustengrav, guarded by however many centuries of Nord dead don't take kindly to visitors. I told Wulfgar I'd stand at her back no matter what waited in that tomb, and I meant every word of it. That's the oath. That's what I'm for. But I won't lie in my own diary — barrows unsettle me more than bandits ever have. Steel and flesh I understand. Whatever's been rotting in a tomb for four thousand years answering back when you open the door, that's a different fight, and not one shield and sword always answer for.\n\nFaendal left us there. Dismissed, and off to Riverwood without much ceremony. Can't say I'll miss the constant Bosmer commentary on everything from wolves to the afterlife, but he pulled his weight when it mattered — coordinated fire is coordinated fire, elf or no. Just Jules and me now, which suits me fine. Fewer voices to manage, and I trust my own read of a fight better than trying to guess what a hunter three paces back is planning.\n\nComing down off the mountain we ran into a troll near dusk two nights back — ugly, fast, regenerates faster than you can carve into it. Jules staggered it with the Voice before it got its claws into either of us, Faendal put an arrow through its neck, and I finished the job with the axe. Good work, all three of us moving like we'd drilled it. Then bears at Pinepeak Cavern — two of the damn things, one right at the mouth of the cave and another waiting inside like it knew we were coming. Bears are worse than trolls in some ways, meaner up close, and that cave stank of old blood and worse before we even cleared it. We came out the other side with a book on armor forging, which Jules seemed pleased about, and not a scratch between us. I'll take that trade every time.\n\nSlept properly last night for the first time in what feels like a week — actual furs, actual roof, actual quiet but for Bassianus complaining at everyone who so much as looked at him. Woke to the whole town chattering about wolves and bears and some haunted barrow east of here that old Wilhelm won't shut up about warning travelers off. Temba's more worried about her timber than any of it, which tells you something about how folk here rank their troubles. I told the guard outside I wouldn't mind a proper bed myself before we climb again — and gods, I meant it. My feet have earned a rest more than most days I can remember, between the road from Darkwater and that mountain path.\n\nSo here's where I've landed on all this, turning it over: I came into this service half-expecting routine guard duty with occasional excitement, the kind of thing housecarls usually get. Instead I've got a Thane who shouts mountains awake and outruns arrows, and a tomb full of the restless dead waiting on the other side of whatever road we take next. That should worry me more than it does. Instead there's something almost steadying about it — she thanked me on the road after that thief went for her, didn't need to, but she did, and it's little things like that which tell me this isn't a burden I'm carrying alone. Whatever's in Ustengrav, we'll go in together. That's the job. That's the oath. I'll sharpen the axe tonight and stop worrying at what I can't yet see.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 716357.51, "x": 0.6967, "y": 0.3681, "ux": 0.3335, "uy": 0.7366}, {"id": 110, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Some distance from Honeystrand Cave, Ivarstead, Hold: The Rift, Outdoors", "imp": 0.55, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Lydia kills a bear near Honeystrand Cave after screaming in combat—three bears ambushed us on the path. I kill a wolf near Taarengrav Mine shortly after, clean shot, no hesitation. We're making progress toward Ustengrav despite the attacks, but the road feels increasingly hostile.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 719636.6, "x": 1.0, "y": 0.2571, "ux": 0.3461, "uy": 0.6351}, {"id": 111, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "content", "location": "Some distance from Honeystrand Cave, Ivarstead, Outdoors, Hold: The Rift", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought and killed a male bear near Honeystrand Cave in Ivarstead, The Rift, while sprinting to intercept it before it could threaten Jules. Used my Steel Shield and Axe of Whiterun in close combat, finishing the beast with a powerful strike to the neck. Jules praised my performance, calling it 'nice work'—I replied that three bears wouldn't slow us down and earned a warm remark about a meal at the inn. No injuries sustained, full magical energy maintained throughout.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 719687.77, "x": 0.7007, "y": 0.5912, "ux": 0.2684, "uy": 0.5582}, {"id": 112, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "angry", "location": "A fair distance from Falkreath Stormcloak Camp, Sons of Skyrim Military Camp, Outdoors, Hold: Falkreath", "imp": 0.65, "type": "RELATIONSHIP", "content": "Faendal rejoined near Falkreath Stormcloak Camp, claiming he'd been watching the ridgeline. Lydia mocked his presence, Faendal defended his skill, and I snapped at him using a mispronounced name. He retaliated by reminding me he kept me fed, then left. His final words carried bitterness from our Riverwood days.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 722639.66, "x": 0.9137, "y": 0.1802, "ux": 0.2965, "uy": 0.7604}, {"id": 113, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "content", "location": "Helgen, Hold: Falkreath, Outdoors", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought and killed a bandit outlaw in Helgen during an ambush. Jules and I engaged in close combat, dispatching the foe with coordinated strikes. I reminded the bandit he'd face harsher foes than us—Nord pride flaring. No injuries sustained, magic energy intact.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 723035.58, "x": 0.6381, "y": 0.6582, "ux": 0.3992, "uy": 0.6529}, {"id": 114, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Sleeping Giant Inn, Riverwood", "imp": 0.7, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Standing guard in the Sleeping Giant Inn, Riverwood, as Dagoth Ur mocks Jules and threatens to burn the inn down. Delphine warns Jules not to trust him, hand on her blade, while Sven sings pro-Imperial ballads nearby. Tension is high—Dagoth Ur's power is unknown, but his disrespect and instability make him a threat. I stay close to Jules, ready to draw my Axe of Whiterun if needed.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 737198.3, "x": 0.5334, "y": 0.5469, "ux": 0.2733, "uy": 0.9842}, {"id": 115, "actor": "Orgnar", "emotion": "disgusted", "location": "Sleeping Giant Inn, Hold: Riverwood", "imp": 0.8, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Dagoth Ur, a red-eyed Dunmer in a bronze mask, arrived at the Sleeping Giant Inn claiming godhood and antagonized Delphine by threatening to burn the inn down twice. He mocked her mead and refused to pay for drinks, speaking in chaotic, vulgar bursts while Jules recruited him as a companion. Sven performed pro-Imperial ballads nearby, ignoring the tension. Delphine warned Jules that Dagoth Ur is dangerous and unhinged, while Lydia defended Jules after she insulted Sven.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 736536.24, "x": 0.506, "y": 0.3934, "ux": 0.2841, "uy": 0.9994}, {"id": 116, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "amused", "location": "Sleeping Giant Inn in Riverwood", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At Sleeping Giant Inn in Riverwood, Delphine threatens me after I mock her watered-down mead and claim I'd burn the inn down—twice. Sven performs a pro-Imperial ballad while I heckle him as a 'mudblood bard.' Jules asks if I'm ready, and I hand her a spell tome to summon me if I glitch into geometry again. Lydia mentions Amber's Shard, an ancient Blight relic, but I dismiss it as forgotten lore.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 736536.24, "x": 0.5712, "y": 0.1433, "ux": 0.2775, "uy": 0.9766}, {"id": 117, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "surprised", "location": "Sleeping Giant Inn in Riverwood", "imp": 0.7, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At the Sleeping Giant Inn in Riverwood, I recruited Dagoth Ur, a masked Dunmer who claims godhood and speaks in chaotic rants, after he threatened to burn the inn down. Delphine warned me he was dangerous and unpaid, while Sven performed Imperial ballads in the corner. I confronted Sven, calling him a wench before leaving; Lydia questioned Amber's Shard, confusing it with Embershard Mine. Dagoth Ur followed me out, yelling about nacho fries returning at Taco Bell.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 732464.73, "x": 0.6053, "y": 0.2485, "ux": 0.2898, "uy": 0.9959}, {"id": 118, "actor": "Delphine", "emotion": "angry", "location": "Sleeping Giant Inn, Riverwood", "imp": 0.8, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Dagoth Ur, the masked Dunmer in a loincloth, threatened to burn down the Sleeping Giant Inn twice today. Warned Jules not to trust him after he mocked me for watering down mead. Sven sang Imperial propaganda songs while Dagoth Ur insulted the Nerevarine and claimed godhood. Tension spiked when I drew my blade's presence as a warning—he laughed and called me a hag.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 736536.24, "x": 0.5167, "y": 0.3592, "ux": 0.2811, "uy": 1.0}, {"id": 119, "actor": "Dorthe", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Riverwood Outskirts, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.65, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Jules questioned me suspiciously about Papa's forge, so I told her to check it herself — I know there's nothing strange there. Later, I saw the red-eyed Dunmer in the bronze mask mocking Lydia near the outskirts, boasting about killing gods and turning bandits to ash. He frightens me, but I won't show it. Frodnar says he talks like a madman, but the way Lydia stands ready with her axe tells me she takes him seriously.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 748697.85, "x": 0.7384, "y": 0.4089, "ux": 0.2501, "uy": 0.4843}, {"id": 120, "actor": "Sven", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Sleeping Giant Inn in Riverwood", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At the Sleeping Giant Inn in Riverwood, I performed my pro-Imperial ballad just as Jules insulted me and stormed out. Dagoth Ur, the masked madman in a loincloth, responded with crude banter while Delphine threatened to kill him if he burned down her inn. Lydia confronted me about Amber's Shard, making me uneasy with her axe at hand. I snapped back that a bard's words outweigh steel, but kept my distance—things felt tense, strange, and volatile.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 736536.24, "x": 0.6033, "y": 0.2822, "ux": 0.2787, "uy": 0.9764}, {"id": 121, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "angry", "location": "Riverwood, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.6, "type": "RELATIONSHIP", "content": "Sprinting through Riverwood with Jules and Lydia after clearing Embershard Mine of bandits. Mocked Lydia's 'bad feeling' and boasted of unmaking gods while she dismissed my claims as drunken wind. Told Jules I'd fuck myself if she wouldn't, then warned her 'they are listening' — possibly the Tribunal, possibly just paranoia. Confronted by Lydia about deeds versus words near Whiterun's military camp, promised to roast the next bandit alive to prove my worth.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 748080.37, "x": 0.8788, "y": 0.4949, "ux": 0.32, "uy": 0.6663}, {"id": 122, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Embershard Mine, Hold: Falkreath", "imp": 0.7, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In Embershard Mine near Riverwood, I killed a Bandit Outlaw who threatened Jules, stepping in with shield raised and axe drawn. The fight was brief but tense—Jules finished another bandit moments later. Dagoth Ur mocked our 'bad feelings' and boasted of god-killing feats, but I stood my ground. We cleared the mine, though the place still feels ill-omened.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 743333.04, "x": 0.76, "y": 0.5325, "ux": 0.3951, "uy": 0.6791}, {"id": 123, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Embershard Mine, Hold: Falkreath", "imp": 0.65, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In Embershard Mine near Falkreath, Lydia and I fought and killed two bandits who ambushed us. Dagoth Ur accompanied us, mocking the danger and boasting of past deeds. After the fight, Lydia urged me to rest before continuing toward Ustengrav. The mine felt claustrophobic, the air thick with dust and tension.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 748164.74, "x": 0.9348, "y": 0.1775, "ux": 0.3394, "uy": 0.7172}, {"id": 124, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Some distance from Whiterun Military Camp, Skyrim, Outdoors", "imp": 0.65, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Confronted Dagoth Ur near Whiterun Military Camp after he provoked me with boasts of divinity and destruction. Challenged him to prove his claims, hand on Axe of Whiterun, but stood down when Jules intervened. Tension remained high as he mocked Nords and lamented the absence of Taco Bell in Skyrim. Later, spoke with a Whiterun guard who noted recent bandit clearings east of the hold.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 759503.79, "x": 0.8253, "y": 0.5087, "ux": 0.1596, "uy": 0.6966}, {"id": 125, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "angry", "location": "Some distance from Whiterun Military Camp, Skyrim, Outdoors; The Bannered Mare, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.55, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At Whiterun Military Camp, Lydia challenges me to prove my boasts in combat, sneering that deeds win wars, not words. I respond that I am the deed itself—mountains remember my name—and ignite flames in my fists, taunting her to draw steel. Jules watches, amused, as the tension builds, but no blades are drawn. Later, at The Bannered Mare, I lament the absence of Taco Bell in Skyrim, comparing it to the spiritual poverty of the Nords.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 761377.09, "x": 0.9278, "y": 0.3158, "ux": 0.2937, "uy": 0.6834}, {"id": 126, "actor": "Unknown", "emotion": "surprised", "location": "Close to Jorrvaskr, Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.8, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Witnessed Jules challenge Nazeem to a duel near Jorrvaskr. She beheaded him in one strike with her Ancient Nord Greatsword. Crowd gathered but no one intervened—clearly saw it as fair. Reported the incident to Commander Caius; he called it 'clean justice.'", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 805212.87, "x": 0.5327, "y": 0.7563, "ux": 0.0069, "uy": 0.5386}, {"id": 127, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Close to Jorrvaskr, Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.65, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Sprint through Whiterun with Jules after Dagoth Ur's crude outburst near Jorrvaskr. Eris joins the group, her blindness noted but not limiting her presence. Dagoth Ur rants about mason jars and Dibella, then threatens to test alchemical insults. I keep my hand near my axe, wary of his instability and protective of my Thane.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 803342.29, "x": 0.7508, "y": 0.62, "ux": 0.149, "uy": 0.6584}, {"id": 128, "actor": "Brenuin", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Bannered Mare in Whiterun", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Hulda tells Jules she's selling The Bannered Mare to Ysolda and is ready to retire. Mikael sings his usual Imperial war ballads to indifferent patrons. Jon Battle-Born mocks Mikael's repetitive songs, calling them tiresome after three winters. Hulda admits she keeps Mikael only because replacing him costs gold.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 769101.86, "x": 0.6295, "y": 0.4158, "ux": 0.3793, "uy": 0.9616}, {"id": 129, "actor": "Unknown", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Bannered Mare, Whiterun", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Overheard Jon Battle-Born grumbling to Hulda at the Bannered Mare about Mikael's tired war songs mocking Ulfric Stormcloak - three winters running the same set. Hulda agreed she'd silence him if replacing a bard didn't cost so much. Meanwhile Jules rented a room from Hulda for the night. Just background noise while I kept to my own business.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 769101.86, "x": 0.5639, "y": 0.39, "ux": 0.3788, "uy": 0.9616}, {"id": 130, "actor": "Lucia", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Bannered Mare, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Spent an evening near the Bannered Mare listening to Mikael drone on about Imperials and Stormcloaks while Hulda and Jon Battle-Born complained about his tired singing. Heard Hulda mention she might sell the inn to Ysolda when she retires. Nothing came my way - no coin, no food offered - just background noise of adults talking business and politics that don't concern me.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 769101.86, "x": 0.6695, "y": 0.2108, "ux": 0.3713, "uy": 0.968}, {"id": 131, "actor": "Mikael", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Bannered Mare, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "I performed my usual set at the Bannered Mare - Ragnar the Red and my anti-Ulfric ballad about the children of Skyrim. Jules showed up and recruited some hooded Altmer woman named Eris as a companion right there in the tavern, swearing oaths of bound fate or some nonsense. Eris made a snide remark about a 'tryst' teaching a woman a lesson - didn't catch the full context, none of my business. Kept playing through it all, my music never stops for anyone.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 803342.29, "x": 0.626, "y": 0.3294, "ux": 0.1934, "uy": 0.4078}, {"id": 132, "actor": "Commander Caius", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Whiterun, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.3, "type": "KNOWLEDGE", "content": "Overheard Lydia telling Farengar that 'm'lady' has coin from a dragon parts sale - Jules, no doubt, still flush from dealing with the court wizard. Also caught the usual noise around the market: Anoriath pitching game meat, Ysolda angling for venison stew. Nothing urgent, but I note Jules's growing wealth and connections in Dragonsreach - worth watching given the Nazeem business.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 807254.02, "x": 0.7828, "y": 0.3375, "ux": 0.1483, "uy": 0.5059}, {"id": 133, "actor": "Ysolda", "emotion": "content", "location": "Whiterun, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Chatted with Anoriath at his market stall about venison for a stew recipe I want to try - offered a hot bowl in trade if he brings fresh game quick. Spent the morning near Jorrvaskr studying the marketplace stalls as usual, sharpening my sense of trade. Heard Hulda's still fending off Mikael's endless war ballads at the Mare, and Jon Battle-Born grumbling about the same tired tune. Ordinary day, but every hour at the stalls gets me closer to running my own inn someday.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 769101.86, "x": 0.6784, "y": 0.2394, "ux": 0.3608, "uy": 0.958}, {"id": 134, "actor": "Carlotta Valentia", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Bannered Mare, Whiterun", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Overheard Mikael droning his same tired Imperial war ballad at the Bannered Mare again - three years running the same tune according to Jon Battle-Born, who'd finally had enough of it. Hulda agreed she'd sack him if a replacement bard didn't cost so much. A Breton traveler rented a room for the night while Ysolda lingered near the market stalls the next morning, saying she's studying merchants to run an inn herself someday. Nothing unusual, just another evening listening to Mikael's insufferable singing.", "day": "25th of Last Seed", "gt": 769101.86, "x": 0.6705, "y": 0.1899, "ux": 0.3739, "uy": 0.9709}, {"id": 135, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "content", "location": "The Bannered Mare, Hold: Whiterun", "imp": 0.5, "type": "RELATIONSHIP", "content": "Recruited Eris, a blind Altmer mercenary, as a companion at the Bannered Mare in Whiterun - she speaks in old, measured cadences and claims her sight loss sharpened her other senses. Spent the day around Whiterun: Dagoth Ur pestered Eris about mysterious alchemical schemes involving a Dibella statue, which I refused to help with. Bought a Common Soul Gem from Farengar at Dragonsreach for 126 gold, then sold a haul of pelts and jewelry to Ulfberth War-Bear at Warmaiden's for 200 gold. Lydia and Eris traded barbed but good-natured banter throughout - my little band is growing stranger by the day.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 803342.29, "x": 0.8615, "y": 0.1972, "ux": 0.1805, "uy": 0.5896}, {"id": 136, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Bannered Mare in Whiterun", "imp": 0.6, "type": "RELATIONSHIP", "content": "Jules approached me at the Bannered Mare in Whiterun and, unlike most, did not press about my hood or my eyes. I named myself Eris, the last standing among many, and swore my oath to travel with them. Since then we've moved through Whiterun together - past Jorrvaskr, Dragonsreach, Arcadia's Cauldron, Warmaiden's - while Lydia bristled at Dagoth Ur's talk of mason jars and Dibella statues, and the ash-blood needled me about old smoke he claims still clings to me. I said little of my past and gave nothing away; some things are mine alone to carry.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 803342.29, "x": 0.6326, "y": 0.5637, "ux": 0.1686, "uy": 0.5498}, {"id": 137, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "amused", "location": "The Bannered Mare in Whiterun", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Watched Jules recruit some blind hooded Altmer edgelord named Eris at The Bannered Mare in Whiterun — claims to be 'the last standing among many,' talks like a haunted fortune cookie. Got excited when Lydia mentioned Eris smells like a repressed alchemist who's brewed dark rites before; tried to recruit her into my foreskin catalyst project with a Dibella statue and mason jar, she deflected hard. Jules refused to buy me the jar, called me 'Dagoff,' so I'm improvising with garlic and spite like always. Spent the rest of the day trailing the party through Whiterun's markets while Lydia and Eris traded barbed non-answers about desperation and rites best left to gods.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 803342.29, "x": 0.6658, "y": 0.4244, "ux": 0.1724, "uy": 0.5391}, {"id": 138, "actor": "Adrianne Avenicci", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Whiterun, near the Door to Warmaiden's, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Overheard strange goings-on near my shop today - a masked Dunmer called Dagoth Ur pestering that hooded Altmer woman Eris about statues and jars, going on about some ash-blood alchemy nonsense. Later a Bosmer hunter, Faendal, showed up demanding fifty gold from the Breton woman Jules over some old debt and grudge - she paid him off just to be rid of him. Strange folk passing through Whiterun lately, none of them customers. Kept my head down and stayed near Warmaiden's.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 808306.65, "x": 0.7934, "y": 0.3007, "ux": 0.1903, "uy": 0.5951}, {"id": 139, "actor": "Unknown", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Whiterun, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Quiet patrol through Whiterun's Plains District - overheard Dagoth Ur badgering Jules for some jar again near Warmaiden's, and Lydia trading barbs with the hooded woman Eris about garlic and spite. Later that Bosmer hunter Faendal turned up asking for Jules directly, muttering about being told to 'fuck off' back on some road, clearly still stinging from it. Ysolda promised stew for a quick errand, Lillith Maiden-Loom teased me about doing my good deed for the day. Nothing dangerous, just the usual strange company Jules keeps.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 807577.35, "x": 0.7114, "y": 0.6159, "ux": 0.1974, "uy": 0.5127}, {"id": 140, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Whiterun, near the Door to Warmaiden's, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.35, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Trailed my Thane through Whiterun's shops today - Farengar's enchantments in Dragonsreach, Arcadia's tonics, then Ulfberth War-Bear's forge at Warmaiden's where Jules sold off pelts and jewelry for 200 gold. Faendal showed up outside Warmaiden's still nursing a grudge over Jules telling him to fuck off back on the road, demanding coin owed for arrows and honor. Jules paid him 50 gold to settle it, still mangling his name as 'FanDoll.' Eris and Dagoth Ur traded barbs with the wood elf and each other the whole time - Dagoth needling Eris about ash and old grief, her firing back a warning about ash that still remembers how to burn. Kept my eyes open through it all; more theater than threat, but I don't trust that Dunmer's tongue.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 811367.39, "x": 0.6402, "y": 0.454, "ux": 0.1827, "uy": 0.6017}, {"id": 141, "actor": "Braith", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Whiterun, near the Door to Warmaiden's, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "I snapped at some elder who was staring at me near the Wind District, told them I wasn't scared even if they were older than me. Later, near Warmaiden's, I overheard some wood elf named Faendal confront a Breton woman about telling him to 'fuck off' on some road, real dramatic stuff. A hooded elder woman named Eris got involved too, saying something about wounds following strikers across Skyrim. Grown-ups and their messy business - none of them even noticed me listening in.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 810318.05, "x": 0.7819, "y": 0.2343, "ux": 0.22, "uy": 0.3723}, {"id": 142, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Whiterun, near the Door to Warmaiden's, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Faendal followed me from Riverwood to Whiterun to confront me over telling him to 'fuck off' - still smarting over the Camilla situation. I paid him 50 gold to settle the debt of arrows and honor he claimed I owed, still mangling his name as 'FanDoll' just to needle him. Eris and Dagoth Ur bickered the whole time, trading barbs about ash, grief, and his unhinged talk of Daedra hedge funds and Nocturnal feet pics. Afterward I hired Bjorlam's carriage at Whiterun Stables for 60 gold and set off toward Solitude to finally pursue the Bard's College.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 816248.36, "x": 0.825, "y": 0.2651, "ux": 0.1529, "uy": 0.6172}, {"id": 143, "actor": "Lillith Maiden-Loom", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Whiterun, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Spent the day about Whiterun observing the usual mix of oddballs and gossips. A masked Dunmer calling himself Dagoth Ur rambled to Jules about jars, garlic, and some nonsense about feet pics and hedge funds - Lydia and a hooded Altmer named Eris traded barbs with him near Jorrvaskr. Overheard Ysolda at the market saying she studies the stalls to learn trading, hoping to run an inn someday - shrewd girl, worth watching. Mikael butchered another verse of Ragnar the Red at the Bannered Mare as usual. Nothing of real business consequence, but I keep my ears open all the same.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 809688.46, "x": 0.8833, "y": 0.3492, "ux": 0.152, "uy": 0.6397}, {"id": 144, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Whiterun Stables, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Faendal followed Jules from Riverwood to Whiterun over an old slight, demanding coin and courtesy owed - Jules paid him fifty gold near Warmaiden's and the debt was settled, though he still mangles his own name for her. Dagoth Ur pestered me twice, first sniffing out 'ash and burnt oath' from my past, which I rebuffed sharply, then rambling about Nocturnal and hedge funds until I questioned why no one has struck him yet. Jules hired Bjorlam's carriage at Whiterun Stables for sixty gold, bound for Solitude. We are now travelling northwest, hours from Whiterun, nearing Katla's Farm outside Solitude.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 816248.36, "x": 0.6942, "y": 0.5834, "ux": 0.1372, "uy": 0.5926}, {"id": 145, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Whiterun, near the Door to Warmaiden's, Hold: Whiterun, Outdoors", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Faendal chased Jules all the way to Whiterun over 'fuck off,' Eris needling him about a debt of arrows and honor until Jules paid him 50 gold to shut it down. I sniffed grief and old ash off Eris outside Warmaiden's — she warned me not to sniff too close, cryptic little pyre. Pitched Nerevar my Nocturnal feet-pics-to-East-Empire-stock arbitrage thesis, Eris questioned why my mouth hasn't been struck off yet, I reminded her I survived a sword through my soul. Jules hired Bjorlam's carriage from Whiterun Stables and we rode all the way out to Solitude, ending up near Katla's Farm — new city, new troglodytes to catalogue.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 816248.36, "x": 0.5991, "y": 0.6499, "ux": 0.1862, "uy": 0.5468}, {"id": 146, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "sad", "location": "Solitude, Hold: Haafingar, Outdoors", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Rode Bjorlam's carriage from Whiterun to Solitude with Jules, arriving late to find the city gathered for an execution. Watched Roggvir beheaded before the crowd for opening the gate to let Ulfric Stormcloak escape after he killed High King Torygg - Roggvir claimed it was fair combat under Nord tradition, but the crowd jeered him as a traitor. Little Svari cried for her uncle while her father Addvar dragged her away, and Eris offered the dying guard a strange blessing toward Sovngarde. Jules and I retreated to the Winking Skeever for the night, unsettled - even Dagoth Ur's usual nonsense couldn't lighten the mood.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 819482.05, "x": 0.5981, "y": 0.548, "ux": 0.1293, "uy": 0.3538}, {"id": 147, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Solitude, Hold: Haafingar", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "I witnessed Roggvir's execution outside Solitude's gates - a guard beheaded for opening the gates to let Ulfric Stormcloak escape after his duel with High King Torygg. The crowd jeered; Jala and Sorex Vinius booed while Beirand alone said he died well. I offered him words of fair travel to Sovngarde as the axe fell - a quiet death made loud by the mob's spectacle. Afterward Jules led us to the Winking Skeever, where we rested; Corpulus Vinius rented us a room and warned of Ustengrav's lingering chill, which Jules means to brave regardless.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 860119.99, "x": 0.6018, "y": 0.5375, "ux": 0.1341, "uy": 0.3341}, {"id": 148, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "traumatized", "location": "Solitude, Hold: Haafingar", "imp": 0.75, "type": "TRAUMA", "content": "Witnessed Roggvir's execution outside Solitude's gates - Captain Aldis condemned him for opening the city to Ulfric Stormcloak after Torygg's death. Roggvir spoke of Nord custom and Sovngarde before Ahtar's axe fell; the crowd (Jala, Vivienne, Sorex) jeered while Svari begged her father Addvar to save her uncle. Eris called it a loud death for a quiet crime - I felt sick watching grief dressed up as justice. Retreated to the Winking Skeever with Eris and Lydia, rented a room, ate cabbage soup, and slept - woke resolved to finally push on toward Ustengrav.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 860119.99, "x": 0.7246, "y": 0.3303, "ux": 0.137, "uy": 0.3293}, {"id": 149, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "disgusted", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Watched Solitude execute Roggvir outside the city gates for opening the door to let Ulfric escape after the High King's death — Svari begged them to spare her uncle, Sorex Vinius sneered 'get on with it,' and Eris offered the man a cold blessing toward Sovngarde as the axe fell. I cracked a Discord-leak joke to Nerevar mid-execution because someone had to lighten the mood of a bunch of Nords cheering their own guardsman's death. Afterward Jules led us to the Winking Skeever in Solitude, rented a room from Corpulus Vinius, and I got to marinate in Lisette's insufferable Dragonborn ballad all night. Come morning Jules bought cabbage potato soup and started plotting a trip to Ustengrav while Lydia grumbled about tomb-chills — mortal logistics, tedious as ever.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 860119.99, "x": 0.6145, "y": 0.3539, "ux": 0.1586, "uy": 0.3345}, {"id": 150, "actor": "Beirand", "emotion": "sad", "location": "Solitude, Hold: Haafingar", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Witnessed Roggvir's execution outside Solitude - Captain Aldis condemned him for opening the gate that let Ulfric Stormcloak escape after killing High King Torygg. Roggvir stood by his choice, calling it Nord tradition, before Ahtar's axe fell. I said only 'He died well' - a guardsman's honor mattered more to me than the politics of it. Later that same day, the hooded traveler Jules came by my forge to browse weapons and armor, business as usual despite the grim morning.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 860697.51, "x": 0.6201, "y": 0.521, "ux": 0.1281, "uy": 0.3413}, {"id": 151, "actor": "Taarie", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Solitude, Hold: Haafingar, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Witnessed Roggvir's execution outside in Solitude - he declared he'd go to Sovngarde for upholding Nord tradition before the axe fell. The crowd was divided: Sorex Vinius and Vivienne Onis cheered his death as deserved, while Greta and Beirand mourned him as a man who died well but shouldn't have had to. I stood by my belief that his treason in aiding Ulfric's escape warranted this justice, though the raw grief in the crowd was hard to ignore. Jala booed the proceedings while the odd hooded woman Eris mused about mobs delighting in death.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 861084.2, "x": 0.6629, "y": 0.3364, "ux": 0.1259, "uy": 0.336}, {"id": 152, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Spent the morning in Solitude with Jules. Corpulus Vinius warned us about the chill in Ustengrav and sold her cabbage potato soup at the Winking Skeever - I agreed old Nord ruins earn their reputation. Jules applied to the Bards College, and Viarmo tasked her with retrieving King Olaf's Verse from Dead Man's Respite to convince Jarl Elisif to lift her ban on the Burning of King Olaf festival. Later she bought supplies from Beirand the blacksmith. Ustengrav weighs on my mind - the Greybeards' trial for the horn awaits, and now this errand for the bards besides.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 893323.61, "x": 0.4264, "y": 0.3922, "ux": 0.2912, "uy": 0.3374}, {"id": 153, "actor": "Lisette", "emotion": "sad", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "I performed my Dragonborn ballad through the night at the Winking Skeever, watching a traveler named Jules check bounties with Corpulus and later rent a room. Earlier that evening I witnessed Roggvir's execution outside the city - Captain Aldis condemned him for helping Ulfric escape after killing High King Torygg, and the crowd was split between jeers from Jala and Vivienne and grief from Svari and Greta. By morning I'd moved on to a new composition honoring the Imperial Legion, while mercenaries Belrand and Lydia traded talk of draugr and old ruins over breakfast. The execution still weighs on me - another piece of Skyrim's history I'll need to chronicle properly.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 860396.35, "x": 0.7006, "y": 0.3026, "ux": 0.1837, "uy": 0.3659}, {"id": 154, "actor": "Svari", "emotion": "traumatized", "location": "Solitude, Hold: Haafingar", "imp": 0.9, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "I begged Papa to save Uncle Roggvir before the crowd, but he told me to go home and wait for Mama. Jala shouted 'You betrayed us!' and Sorex Vinius called for the execution to proceed. Vivienne Onis told Papa he should just tell me my uncle was scum who betrayed the High King - right in front of me. I didn't go straight home; I lingered near the sewers entrance, feeling numb and small amid all the people who hated my uncle.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 860396.35, "x": 0.6337, "y": 0.3605, "ux": 0.1376, "uy": 0.3307}, {"id": 155, "actor": "Jaree-Ra", "emotion": "angry", "location": "Solitude, near the Entrance to Solitude Sewers, Hold: Haafingar", "imp": 0.9, "type": "TRAUMA", "content": "Guards arrested me at Solitude, right near the sewers where I make my pitches. I'd just laid out the Icerunner scheme to that Breton woman, Jules - the lighthouse fire, the shipwreck, the easy gold - and someone must have talked. Now I'm cuffed and marched toward Castle Dour, no chance to run or fight, just my tongue left to work with. Deeja will need to know what happened - I hope she's not next.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 863340.41, "x": 0.5858, "y": 0.3871, "ux": 0.2912, "uy": 0.4114}, {"id": 156, "actor": "Fihada", "emotion": "content", "location": "Castle Fletcher, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "A Breton adventurer named Jules browsed my shop at Castle Fletcher and I greeted her with my usual pitch - pegged her for an archer straight away. She opened a trade with me before heading off, saying she might return. Same morning, that mercenary Belrand was at the Winking Skeever needling me about arrows not being enough against draugr, going on about his own steel-and-spellwork combo. I let it slide with a smile - competition for attention is nothing new at Corpulus's tavern.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 860697.51, "x": 0.7139, "y": 0.6152, "ux": 0.2254, "uy": 0.5792}, {"id": 157, "actor": "Jordis the Sword-Maiden", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Passed through the Winking Skeever and heard Lisette singing the Dragonborn ballad again - word's spreading fast about the Breton woman who slew a dragon. Overheard talk of Ustengrav and old Nord ruins from a housecarl and her Thane at Corpulus Vinius's tables. Nothing that concerns me directly, but Solitude feels tense these days with Legion patrols on edge over Thalmor troubles near Dragon Bridge.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 863340.41, "x": 0.7126, "y": 0.2088, "ux": 0.2121, "uy": 0.3348}, {"id": 158, "actor": "Minette Vinius", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Da checked in a Breton traveler named Jules who rented a room and bought bounty info, then came back later for soup and to check our wares. Lisette sang her Dragonborn ballad again all night - I still think that traveler might be her. Overheard Belrand bragging to Fihada the fletcher about his swordwork being better than arrows against draugr. Nothing I haven't seen a hundred times at the Skeever, but I like watching Da work the room.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 863340.41, "x": 0.716, "y": 0.4092, "ux": 0.2171, "uy": 0.5034}, {"id": 159, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "angry", "location": "Solitude, Hold: Haafingar, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In Solitude, Jaree-Ra the Argonian tried recruiting Jules into a scheme to douse the Solitude Lighthouse and wreck the Icerunner for salvage. Dagoth Ur argued for turning him in rather than risk Thalmor attention, and Jules reported him to a Solitude Guard, who dispatched men to arrest Jaree-Ra. Dagoth Ur mouthed off again near the crowd talking about dragons at Whiterun, and I threatened him twice - once over his crude jokes, once when he mocked the guards - a guard had to order us both to stand down before blades were drawn.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 900155.1, "x": 0.6399, "y": 0.5526, "ux": 0.3002, "uy": 0.3936}, {"id": 160, "actor": "Unknown", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Solitude, near the Entrance to Solitude Sewers, Hold: Haafingar, Outdoors", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "I intervened when a Whiterun housecarl, Lydia, drew steel on some elf near the courtyard, threatening to spill blood over an argument. I ordered them both to stand down and hold their tongues - won't have violence in Solitude's streets. Earlier that woman traveling with a steel-armored companion reported a crime to me, and I noted her fine steel gear before hearing her out. I also overheard that shifty Argonian, Jaree-Ra, near the sewer entrance trying to talk someone into 'easy gold' - treasure hunting talk that smells like thievery to me.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 894446.36, "x": 0.9849, "y": 0.2687, "ux": 0.2753, "uy": 0.665}, {"id": 161, "actor": "Noster Eagle-Eye", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Solitude, Hold: Haafingar, Outdoors", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Watched Roggvir get executed at the chopping block near the city gate - the gate guard who let Ulfric escape after killing High King Torygg. Jala and Vivienne Onis cheered his death while Svari, his niece, begged Addvar to save him. I called out to a passing woman for a septim or two, same as always - most just walked past like they always do. Heard talk of an Argonian named Jaree-Ra scheming to sabotage a lighthouse for the ship Icerunner, and a Solitude Guard got sent to arrest him near the sewers entrance.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 860396.35, "x": 0.7365, "y": 0.3924, "ux": 0.1233, "uy": 0.3326}, {"id": 162, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Solitude, Hold: Haafingar, Outdoors", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In Solitude, Jules took Viarmo's task at the Bards College: recover King Olaf's Verse from Dead Man's Respite to sway Jarl Elisif on lifting her ban of the Burning of King Olaf festival. We visited Beirand's smithy and Fihada's fletchery for supplies, then the Argonian Jaree-Ra propositioned Jules near the sewers to douse the Solitude Lighthouse and wreck the Icerunner for profit. Dagoth Ur argued for turning him in rather than risking Thalmor attention, and after Lydia snapped at his crudeness twice, Jules reported Jaree-Ra to a guard who dispatched men to arrest him. I said little through it all, though the college's silence and the mercenary's greed both struck me as worth noting.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 896142.51, "x": 0.3694, "y": 0.4725, "ux": 0.3362, "uy": 0.3598}, {"id": 163, "actor": "Jawanan", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Solitude, Hold: Haafingar, Outdoors", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Walking through Solitude, I overheard Silana Petreia near Angeline's Aromatics speaking about the Divines saving her from the streets. Later near the sewers entrance, Sorex Vinius rebuffed Jaree-Ra's persistent advances, saying he wasn't interested no matter how many times asked. Hours later I noticed a Solitude Guard chatting with a woman in fine steel armor, who told him she wished to report a crime. Just background noise on my walk, but Solitude always has something happening.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 894446.36, "x": 0.7695, "y": 0.2191, "ux": 0.3272, "uy": 0.4828}, {"id": 164, "actor": "Unknown", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At the Winking Skeever I overheard a stranger called Jules haggling with Corpulus over bounties, mage dens, and a room for the night - typical tavern business. Outside near the inn door, that unsettling masked Dunmer who calls himself Dagoth Ur mocked an Argonian to turn over to the Legion, then goaded Lydia into drawing her axe on him. A Solitude guard was rattling on about dragons attacking Whiterun and some 'Dragonborn' - more wild talk to add to the pile. None of it concerns me directly, but Solitude's gotten strange lately.", "day": "26th of Last Seed", "gt": 863340.41, "x": 0.7725, "y": 0.3116, "ux": 0.24, "uy": 0.4473}, {"id": 165, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "amused", "location": "Solitude, Hold: Haafingar, Outdoors", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Jules applies to the Bards College in Solitude — Viarmo tasks her with recovering King Olaf's Verse from Dead Man's Respite to convince Elisif to un-ban the Burning of King Olaf festival. Meanwhile the lizard grifter Jaree-Ra pitches Jules a scheme to douse the Solitude Lighthouse and wreck the Icerunner for salvage; I talked her out of it, arguing the Legion coin scam wasn't worth Thalmor eyes on us, and we snitched on him to the guards instead. Lydia keeps threatening my mask with her axe over my mouth and I keep goading her to swing it. Watched the guards drag Jaree-Ra off on our word while a dragon reportedly eats Whiterun and nobody here seems to care.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 896142.51, "x": 0.4962, "y": 0.4089, "ux": 0.2967, "uy": 0.3711}, {"id": 166, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Solitude, Hold: Haafingar, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Applied to the Bards College in Solitude - Viarmo set my trial: recover King Olaf's Verse, a lost portion of the Poetic Edda, from Dead Man's Respite to help convince Jarl Elisif to allow the Burning of King Olaf festival. Between errands I traded with Beirand and Fihada, then Jaree-Ra propositioned me to sabotage the Solitude Lighthouse and wreck the Icerunner for smuggling profit. Dagoth Ur argued for turning him in to avoid Thalmor scrutiny, Lydia nearly came to blows with him over his mouth, and I reported Jaree-Ra to a Solitude Guard who dispatched men to arrest him. Captain Aldis dismissed my accusation for lack of proof, but the guard confirmed Jaree-Ra was taken in anyway.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 896142.51, "x": 0.4695, "y": 0.1349, "ux": 0.3163, "uy": 0.3673}, {"id": 167, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "angry", "location": "Solitude Jail, Hold: Castle Dour", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Jaree-Ra sits caged in Solitude Jail after Jules turned him in - still smug, taunting us about the Icerunner gold he offered. I threw his own words back at him, reminded him of the sailors who'd have drowned when that lighthouse went dark. Eris weighed in coolly, telling him his own tongue already gave the guards enough truth. Eris also told Jules not to mistreat me, that duty and honor go together - I noted that, unexpected from someone I barely know.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 906858.13, "x": 0.5767, "y": 0.5944, "ux": 0.2973, "uy": 0.404}, {"id": 168, "actor": "Unknown", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Solitude, near the Door to Castle Dour Dungeon, Hold: Haafingar, Outdoors", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Overheard Jules accuse the Argonian Jaree-Ra of plotting a staged shipwreck, but she had no proof to give Captain Aldis outside Castle Dour. Later, near the dungeon door, I found myself commenting to a passerby about fine clothes and Radiant Raiments. Still later, a hooded stranger named Eris warned Jules not to mistreat her housecarl Lydia, praising the honor in Lydia's duty. Routine day patrolling Solitude - nothing that concerns Legion business directly.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 906858.13, "x": 0.5915, "y": 0.5588, "ux": 0.2522, "uy": 0.4255}, {"id": 169, "actor": "Unknown", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Solitude, near the Door to Castle Dour Dungeon, Hold: Haafingar, Outdoors", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Overheard the Breton adventurer confront Captain Aldis near Castle Dour, accusing the Argonian Jaree-Ra of plotting a staged shipwreck. She had no proof, and Aldis rightly turned her away demanding evidence. Later I gave her some passing advice about Radiant Raiments for finer clothes. Afterward, a hooded Altmer woman named Eris warned her not to mistreat her housecarl, invoking honor and duty - words I can respect.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 906858.13, "x": 0.7015, "y": 0.2786, "ux": 0.2223, "uy": 0.4069}, {"id": 170, "actor": "Unknown", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Solitude, Hold: Haafingar, Outdoors", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Overheard the Breton woman Jules accuse Jaree-Ra to Captain Aldis of plotting a staged shipwreck, but she had no proof - Aldis rightly turned her away until she brings evidence. Later near Castle Dour, an Imperial Soldier gave some traveler shopping advice about Radiant Raiments. Still later, a hooded stranger named Eris warned Jules not to mistreat her housecarl, speaking of honor in duty. Kept watch through it all - nothing requiring my intervention, but worth remembering Jaree-Ra's name if trouble follows.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 906858.13, "x": 0.6188, "y": 0.5594, "ux": 0.2384, "uy": 0.4169}, {"id": 171, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "amused", "location": "Solitude Jail, Hold: Castle Dour", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Sprinted through Solitude with Jules to Castle Dour Dungeon, watching her interrogate the caged lizard Jaree-Ra about his Icerunner scheme through the bars. Bjartur the Stormcloak prisoner kept snarling defiance at the Imperial dogs while Eris needled Jaree-Ra about whether his hide's worth more caged than free. Lydia threw the drowning-sailors line back in his scaled face, and I got distracted wondering aloud why every Dunmer baddie's got no daddy when I'm right here. Jules still lacks proof for Captain Aldis outside - typical Legion bureaucracy demanding evidence for crimes not yet committed.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 906957.09, "x": 0.6226, "y": 0.523, "ux": 0.2898, "uy": 0.4132}, {"id": 172, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Solitude Jail, Hold: Castle Dour", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At Solitude Jail in Castle Dour, Jules confronted the caged Jaree-Ra about the Icerunner plot while Lydia sharply reminded him of the sailors his sabotage would have drowned. I told him plainly I was weighing whether his hide serves the guards better than the truth his own tongue already gave them - he needled back, offering to cut a deal instead of rotting in the cage. Jules admitted to Captain Aldis outside they lacked proof to indict him further. Dagoth Ur carried on with his usual noise nearby, and afterward I warned Jules not to mistreat Lydia, who holds honour in her duty as housecarl.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 906957.09, "x": 0.6749, "y": 0.5275, "ux": 0.2862, "uy": 0.4103}, {"id": 173, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "angry", "location": "Solitude Jail, Castle Dour", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "I turned Jaree-Ra in properly this time, tracking him down in Solitude Jail after guards caged him for the Icerunner smuggling plot. I baited him to the cell door repeatedly, taunting him, but he just laughed - claiming words alone aren't a crime and that I'm no less complicit for hearing his numbers. Lydia snapped at him about the sailors who'd drown if the lighthouse went dark, and Eris weighed aloud whether his hide was worth more to the guards than his own confession. I still need harder evidence to see him properly indicted; for now he sits mocking us all from behind bars while Deeja remains free somewhere in the city.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 907490.37, "x": 0.7863, "y": 0.2319, "ux": 0.3106, "uy": 0.3954}, {"id": 174, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "amused", "location": "Meeko's Shack Outskirts, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Jules reads a dead Nord's journal aloud outside Meeko's Shack in Hjaalmarch — some skooma-brained hermit who spent his last days hunting a dog named Meeko and never found him. I riff that at least he wrote his feelings down instead of screaming into the void like me for three millennia, and mention it kept a volcano from collapsing on schedule. Lydia and I trade barbs about grunting Nords versus load-bearing prophecy-screaming; she says some things just need less commentary from me. Jules agrees the sagas she grew up on are basically bears grunting with bad editors.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 920317.43, "x": 0.519, "y": 0.685, "ux": 0.3923, "uy": 0.4966}, {"id": 175, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "content", "location": "Meeko's Shack Outskirts, Hold: Hjaalmarch, Outdoors", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Left Solitude after Jaree-Ra's imprisonment, traveling with Lydia, Eris, and Dagoth Ur through Katla's Farm and toward Hjaalmarch. Passed the Shrine of Meridia and a Stormcloak camp near Haafingar, the road wearing on us all. At an abandoned shack near Meeko's Shack Outskirts I read a hunter's journal about his failed search for a lost dog named Meeko - a whole life reduced to a few worried pages. Dagoth Ur and Lydia bantered about sagas and poetry over it while I reflected on how small, unfinished stories linger in Skyrim's wilds.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 918355.96, "x": 0.7908, "y": 0.2127, "ux": 0.3898, "uy": 0.5339}, {"id": 176, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "content", "location": "Meeko's Shack Outskirts, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Dagoth Ur, unusually, offers me a grudging compliment near the Stormcloak camp beyond Haafingar - calling me 'roughly matched' and admitting I broke Jaree-Ra's spirit with words alone, no fireballs needed. At Meeko's Shack in Hjaalmarch, Jules reads a hunter's abandoned journal aloud - a Nord who died searching for a lost dog named Meeko, his whole life reduced to worried pages. Lydia and Dagoth Ur trade barbs over it, Lydia noting he at least wrote something instead of screaming into the void, Dagoth countering that his screaming held up a volcano. Small, quiet moment on the road; the party's banter easier than usual, even Dagoth's crudeness tempered by something like respect.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 920317.43, "x": 0.6351, "y": 0.4064, "ux": 0.4212, "uy": 0.522}, {"id": 177, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "content", "location": "Meeko's Shack Outskirts, Hold: Hjaalmarch, Outdoors", "imp": 0.25, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Journeyed from Solitude through Katla's Farm and past Forebears' Holdout to Meeko's Shack in Hjaalmarch, at Jules's back the whole way. Jules read a dead Nord's journal about a lost dog named Meeko - Dagoth Ur mocked the man for writing feelings instead of finding a real hobby, and I told him small mercies, at least the man found words instead of screaming into the void for three thousand years like Dagoth does. He and Jules kept trading jabs about Nord sagas and grunting at bears - I warned him not to fix what doesn't need fixing, some things just need less commentary from him. Long day of travel, but the banter kept it light despite Ustengrav still weighing on my mind.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 918355.96, "x": 0.5416, "y": 0.5839, "ux": 0.3888, "uy": 0.5071}, {"id": 178, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Dead Men's Respite, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Recruited Meeko the dog at his old shack in Hjaalmarch after finding his hunter's journal - he's followed me ever since, even into battle. Brought Lydia to Dead Men's Respite to search for King Olaf's Verse; with Dagoth Ur and Eris we cut through waves of draugr, restless draugr, and frostbite spiders in the crypt's corridors. I'm winded and wounded from the fighting - Dagoth Ur cackling about 'chess club' and Saltrice fields the whole time - but we're pushing deeper toward the tomb's heart. Briefly skimmed a book called 'The Buying Game' mid-fight before pocketing it to sort out later.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 931514.67, "x": 0.7331, "y": 0.3664, "ux": 0.4205, "uy": 0.526}, {"id": 179, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "content", "location": "Dead Men's Respite, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Cleared Dead Men's Respite in Hjaalmarch alongside Jules, Lydia, Eris, and Meeko — draugr after draugr fell to my firebolts and Jules's blade while Eris finished off a frostbite spider with cold precision. I cracked chess-club and Saltrice-field jokes over the corpses, Lydia snapped at Meeko for getting underfoot, and Jules paused mid-slaughter to read 'The Buying Game' before pocketing it for later. Eris warned about hesitation and inebriation both being defeat — fitting, since the whole crypt reeked of old bone dust and dead men's pride. Good hunt, minimal effort, the usual tomb-diving choreography.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 931514.67, "x": 0.623, "y": 0.53, "ux": 0.4971, "uy": 0.4657}, {"id": 180, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Dead Men's Respite, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "We push into Dead Men's Respite in Hjaalmarch, cutting through wave after wave of draugr - myself, Jules, Dagoth Ur, and Lydia working as one grim unit. Dagoth Ur crows crude victory quips over each fresh kill while Lydia curses a stumbling Meeko and warns me of a frostbite spider's poisonous spit rather than its fangs - I finish that one myself. Jules presses forward relentlessly despite exhaustion, pocketing some journal mid-fight rather than pausing to read. The dead here fall easily, but the crypt runs deep, and I sense more stepping stones to come before we find what Viarmo's verse demands.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 931514.67, "x": 0.6934, "y": 0.365, "ux": 0.4994, "uy": 0.4726}, {"id": 181, "actor": "Meeko", "emotion": "fearful", "location": "Dead Men's Respite, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Deep in Dead Men's Respite, I fought alongside Jules, Lydia, Eris, and the strange masked Dagoth Ur against wave after wave of draugr and frostbite spiders. I sank my teeth into a restless draugr and helped bring down a frostbite spider myself, proving my worth in the pack. Lydia snapped at me to watch myself and called me a stupid dog when I got underfoot, but she also warned me to save my growling for real threats, which felt oddly protective. The ruin was thick with old Nord dead and worse, but between the four of us and Dagoth Ur's crude battle-shouting, we cleared corridor after corridor.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 931514.67, "x": 0.7161, "y": 0.435, "ux": 0.5051, "uy": 0.4799}, {"id": 182, "actor": "Svaknir", "emotion": "surprised", "location": "Dead Men's Respite, Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "I watch from a distance as Jules and her strange companions, the blind Altmer Eris and the wild-tongued Dagoth Ur, cut through Dead Men's Respite in Hjaalmarch. Draugr fall in waves, restless ones rising again only to be struck down, frostbite spiders and a skeever besides. Dagoth Ur shouts something crude about an 'e-girl' mid-slaughter, and Eris warns of ambushes with her unnerving calm before the killing starts. Jules later pauses to read a book, King Olaf's Verse, amid the carnage - odd, given the crypt still reeks of death around us.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 961240.7, "x": 0.5487, "y": 0.5703, "ux": 0.4685, "uy": 0.4417}, {"id": 183, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Dead Men's Respite, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought through Dead Men's Respite in Hjaalmarch alongside Jules, Eris, Dagoth Ur, and Meeko - waves of draugr, restless draugr, and frostbite spiders in the winding corridors. Warned Eris about a frostbite spider's poison spit and legs rather than its fangs; she finished it clean. Meeko fought better than I expected, downing spiders and draugr himself, though I still growled 'stupid dog' when he got underfoot. Long grinding push through the crypt, seeking King Olaf's Verse for Viarmo's bard errand - Dagoth Ur's usual filth never stopped even mid-battle.", "day": "27th of Last Seed", "gt": 931514.67, "x": 0.5683, "y": 0.3652, "ux": 0.4889, "uy": 0.4708}, {"id": 184, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Dead Men's Respite, Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Deep in Dead Men's Respite with Lydia, Eris, Dagoth Ur, Svaknir, and Meeko, we cut through wave after wave of draugr, restless draugr, and frostbite spiders toward King Olaf's Verse. I read the recovered book mid-fight, then argued with Dagoth Ur about picking locks - he insisted on melting tumblers instead of using picks, brute force over finesse. Svaknir summoned Olaf's restless spirit as more draugr rose against us, forcing another brutal push through fire and steel. I'm bleeding and utterly spent, but we're closing in on whatever waits at this tomb's heart.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 963532.01, "x": 0.6317, "y": 0.2859, "ux": 0.5138, "uy": 0.4373}, {"id": 185, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Dead Men's Respite, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "We cut deep through Dead Men's Respite in Hjaalmarch, wave after wave of draugr, restless dead, and a Nord ghost named Svaknir hunting his old rival Olaf. I fought alongside Jules, Dagoth Ur, Lydia, and Meeko - Dagoth's crude mockery never let up even as he burned through draugr with ease, and Lydia traded barbs with him over lockpicking versus brute force. Jules recovered King Olaf's Verse for Viarmo and read it aloud, while Svaknir aided us against a chest guarded by a soul gem and ruby claw. The dead here are many, but I sense we near whatever answers this crypt still holds.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 963299.16, "x": 0.6458, "y": 0.3697, "ux": 0.5089, "uy": 0.4156}, {"id": 186, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "content", "location": "Dead Men's Respite, Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.35, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Cleared another wave of draugr through Dead Men's Respite with Jules, Lydia, Eris, and Meeko — I torched Restless Draugr after Restless Draugr while Eris cut down her share and Svaknir the ghost-hunter joined the fray chasing his precious Olaf. Jules read King Olaf's Verse aloud for the Bards College quest, and I told her about my peanut butter, jelly, and asshole sandwich potion recipe, which earned me a 'most disgusting thing you've said so far.' She fat-fingered my name as 'Degas' and I corrected her — I've got an ancient title, not a tailor's shop name. Lydia and I traded barbs about lockpicking versus melting Redoran vault doors off their hinges; petty, but I won that one.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 963299.16, "x": 0.653, "y": 0.3936, "ux": 0.4419, "uy": 0.4987}, {"id": 187, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "surprised", "location": "Dead Men's Respite, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought through Dead Men's Respite in Hjaalmarch alongside Jules, Eris, Dagoth Ur, and a stranger named Svaknir seeking vengeance on King Olaf. Waves of draugr fell to our blades - Eris and Dagoth Ur cutting through them with terrifying efficiency while I held my own against Restless Draugr. At the heart of the tomb, Svaknir called forth King Olaf One-Eye himself, and Eris struck the final blow that felled the ancient king. Afterward at the Winking Skeever in Solitude, Jules delivered the recovered verse to Viarmo, who found it too damaged to read - the truth about Olaf's fraudulent dragon-slaying now theirs to reconstruct from fragments.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 969222.79, "x": 0.4931, "y": 0.4257, "ux": 0.5017, "uy": 0.4066}, {"id": 188, "actor": "Meeko", "emotion": "fearful", "location": "Dead Men's Respite, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Followed Jules, Lydia, Eris, Dagoth Ur and Svaknir through Dead Men's Respite in Hjaalmarch. Watched draugr rise from their crypts as Svaknir called out to wake King Olaf - the four of them cut through wave after wave of undead with blade and fire while I stayed close, ears pinned at the noise and dead-thing stench. Eris finally struck down King Olaf One-Eye himself, ending the fight. Lydia called me a stupid dog twice - stung a little, but I stuck near the pack anyway since the danger passed and everyone walked out alive.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 969222.79, "x": 0.6268, "y": 0.4299, "ux": 0.5079, "uy": 0.4199}, {"id": 189, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "surprised", "location": "Dead Men's Respite, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.7, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought through Dead Men's Respite with Lydia, Eris, and Dagoth Ur - draugr swarmed us in waves and I could barely lift my greatsword by the end. King Olaf One-Eye himself rose to defend his tomb, snarling 'Insolent bard, die!' before Eris finally cut him down. Recovered King Olaf's Verse and brought it to Viarmo at the Bards College, who found it incomplete and unreadable in places. We spent the morning inventing plausible history together - Olaf found Numinex asleep rather than defeating him, and convinced Solitude to attack Winterhold rather than reacting to their aggression. Viarmo is heading to court now to present it to Elisif, and wants me there.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 974768.97, "x": 0.4842, "y": 0.1896, "ux": 0.4667, "uy": 0.3951}, {"id": 190, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "amused", "location": "The Bards College, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Torched Restless Draugr after Restless Draugr through Dead Men's Respite with Jules, Lydia, Eris, and Meeko while Svaknir chased his precious Olaf. King Olaf One-Eye himself rose snarling 'Insolent bard, die!' before Eris cleaved him down for good. I threatened the corpse-king with a future Oblivion Crisis before letting him drop, pure theater but I meant every word. Back in Solitude, Jules presented the incomplete Verse to Viarmo, who rewrote Olaf's legend on the spot — turning a dragon-slaying king into a man who found Numinex asleep and bullied Solitude into sacking Winterhold. Watched mortal history get forged in real time to save a festival about burning an effigy; richer irony than anything the Tribunal ever managed.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 974768.97, "x": 0.4171, "y": 0.33, "ux": 0.4793, "uy": 0.3853}, {"id": 191, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Dead Men's Respite, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "We cleared the last of Dead Men's Respite in Hjaalmarch - I struck down King Olaf One-Eye himself after Jules's blade drew his fury, ending the draugr king's ancient reign. Dagoth Ur, Lydia, Svaknir and I fought through waves of restless dead alongside Jules to reach him. Afterward Jules brought the recovered verse to Viarmo at the Bards College in Solitude, and I watched him fabricate a diplomatic history from our whispered guesses - Olaf found the dragon Numinex asleep rather than defeating him, and provoked Winterhold into striking first. A convenient truth, built from silence and fading ink, to save a festival from a dead king's inconvenient legend.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 974768.97, "x": 0.4262, "y": 0.4489, "ux": 0.4896, "uy": 0.3999}, {"id": 192, "actor": "Viarmo", "emotion": "joyful", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.9, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Jules brought me King Olaf's Verse from his tomb, but the copy was damaged and incomplete. Together we reconstructed the missing lines - deciding Olaf found the dragon Numinex asleep rather than defeating him in battle, and that Olaf provoked Solitude into attacking Winterhold rather than the reverse. I presented the restored verse before Jarl Elisif at the Blue Palace, reciting it in full before the court. Elisif was convinced - she declared the festival a true celebration of Solitude and condemnation of false kings, reversing her ban on the Burning of King Olaf.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 982922.69, "x": 0.1779, "y": 0.3045, "ux": 0.3307, "uy": 0.056}, {"id": 193, "actor": "Unknown", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Blue Palace, Solitude, Outdoors, Hold: Haafingar", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "On patrol outside the Blue Palace, I overhear the Breton traveler Jules confront the wood elf Faendal, accusing him of following her - he denies it, claiming coincidence. A hooded Altmer woman named Eris interjects, needling Faendal about how their paths keep crossing suspiciously often. Nothing criminal, but I note the tension between them in case it escalates near the palace grounds.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 986058.41, "x": 0.5541, "y": 0.4182, "ux": 0.2561, "uy": 0.216}, {"id": 194, "actor": "Bryling", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Viarmo of the Bards College presented King Olaf's recovered verse to Jarl Elisif in the Blue Palace, arguing the Burning of King Olaf Festival honors Solitude's defiance against a false, treacherous king. Elisif was convinced and reinstated the festival, rewarding the College and the Breton woman who recovered the poem. Given the Thalmor theft of our defense plans this very morning, I quietly warned a Solitude Guard to keep watch on the doors during the festival preparations - a distracted court is a vulnerable one. Erikur's man Melaran was absent, small mercies there.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 986512.83, "x": 0.0953, "y": 0.0763, "ux": 0.3283, "uy": 0.0387}, {"id": 195, "actor": "Melaran", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Spent the morning observing court at the Blue Palace as Viarmo of the Bards College petitioned Jarl Elisif to reinstate the Burning of King Olaf Festival. He recited a lengthy recovered verse from the Poetic Edda, painting Olaf One-Eye as a fraud who tricked a sleeping dragon rather than defeating one in battle - Elisif was won over and granted the College patronage. The Breton woman Jules, apparently the one who recovered the verse, was thanked profusely by Viarmo and sent to find someone named Jorn to finish festival preparations. Unremarkable morning of court theater, though the poem's mockery of false Nord heroics amused me privately.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 986512.83, "x": 0.1917, "y": 0.1426, "ux": 0.3289, "uy": 0.0368}, {"id": 196, "actor": "Bolgeir Bearclaw", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "The Blue Palace, Solitude", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Viarmo of the Bards College petitioned Jarl Elisif this morning to reinstate the Burning of King Olaf Festival, presenting a recovered verse from the Poetic Edda - a mocking tale of Olaf's cowardice and false glory. Elisif was moved, granted the festival's return, and promised the College patronage. I noted the Breton woman traveling with him, apparently the one who recovered the poem, being thanked and sent to find someone named Jorn to finish the effigy preparations. Bryling quietly warned a guard to watch the doors, worried the Thalmor might exploit the court's distraction with festival matters after this morning's theft of our defense plans - a concern I share given the tensions in the city.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 986512.83, "x": 0.2047, "y": 0.1086, "ux": 0.3195, "uy": 0.0075}, {"id": 197, "actor": "Jarl Elisif the Fair", "emotion": "content", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Viarmo returned to court with King Olaf's Verse, recovered from the bard's tomb, and recited it in full to prove the Burning of King Olaf Festival honors Solitude's defiance rather than glorifying Olaf. I was moved - the poem's condemnation of Olaf as a liar and false conqueror convinced me to reinstate the festival and grant the Bards College a patronage reward. A traveling Breton woman, Jules, apparently helped recover the verse; Viarmo sent her to tell Jorn to finish the effigy preparations. Bryling quietly warned a guard to watch the doors, wary the Thalmor might exploit the festival distraction after stealing our defense plans this morning.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 986512.83, "x": 0.2231, "y": 0.1807, "ux": 0.3157, "uy": 0.0196}, {"id": 198, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "content", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Followed Jules to the Blue Palace as Viarmo presented King Olaf's restored verse to Jarl Elisif, publicly branding Olaf a liar and thief who staged his dragon conquest and provoked Solitude's wrath through cowardice. Elisif accepted it and reinstated the Burning of King Olaf festival, granting the Bards College a reward. Overheard Thane Bryling quietly order a guard to watch the doors, fearing Thalmor agents might strike during the festival distraction after stealing Solitude's defense plans this morning. Faendal turned up again at the palace, trailed us to the Bards College, and finally left after Jules dismissed him - his coin settled, his pride bruised.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 984025.83, "x": 0.0819, "y": 0.3706, "ux": 0.3136, "uy": 0.1233}, {"id": 199, "actor": "Varnius Junius", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "I stand in the Blue Palace and witness Viarmo of the Bards College petition Jarl Elisif to reinstate the Burning of King Olaf Festival, backing his case by reciting King Olaf's long-lost verse recovered from the bard's tomb. Elisif is moved and grants approval plus coin for the College. Falk Firebeard and a Breton woman named Jules look on as the poem unfolds, and afterward Bryling quietly orders the guards to watch the doors, wary the Thalmor might strike while court attention is on festival matters. A Wood Elf hunter, Faendal, wanders in and out exchanging pleasantries with Jules. I say nothing, an outsider watching Solitude's nobility conduct its affairs.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 986512.83, "x": 0.1391, "y": 0.1956, "ux": 0.3417, "uy": 0.0762}, {"id": 200, "actor": "Meeko", "emotion": "content", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Followed Jules from the Bards College into the Blue Palace as the robed man Viarmo sang his verse about King Olaf before the pack-leader Elisif on her throne. The words made the air hum and everyone seemed pleased, so the festival got approved and Jules was sent to tell the woodsmoke-and-straw man Jorn to finish his preparations for tonight. Along the way a wood elf named Faendal kept turning up wherever we went, trailing us to the palace grounds until Jules grew short with him and he stopped following - I caught Eris murmuring something sharp about his path always bending back toward us. Also heard the masked loud one, Dagoth Ur, ranting about lizards and babies again, same unsettling noise as always.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 984025.83, "x": 0.2191, "y": 0.4825, "ux": 0.307, "uy": 0.1602}, {"id": 201, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Blue Palace, Solitude", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In the Blue Palace, I watched Viarmo recite the fabricated verse before Jarl Elisif - Olaf as liar and coward rather than dragon-slayer, a history spun whole from our guesses at Dead Men's Respite. Elisif accepted it without question, lifted her ban, and promised the Bards College patronage; Viarmo credited Jules for the 'recovery.' Bryling quietly warned a guard to watch the doors, fearing Thalmor mischief while the court's attention was on bard nonsense - a reminder the war doesn't pause for festivals. Faendal reappeared afterward seeking Jules out again, was dismissed, and finally left her service outside the Bards College, debt settled and pride intact.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 985595.91, "x": 0.277, "y": 0.3286, "ux": 0.3093, "uy": 0.1486}, {"id": 202, "actor": "Erikur", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Court convenes at the Blue Palace as Viarmo of the Bards College presents King Olaf's recovered verse to Jarl Elisif, arguing the poem exposes Olaf as a liar and coward rather than the dragon-slaying king of legend. Elisif is convinced and reinstates the Burning of King Olaf Festival, granting the College a patronage reward. Bryling quietly instructs a guard to watch the doors during the festival, wary the Thalmor may exploit the distraction after stealing our defense plans this morning. I note the Bosmer hunter lingering about court, and Falk keeping his usual dry watch over Viarmo's petitions.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 986512.83, "x": 0.1348, "y": 0.0624, "ux": 0.3269, "uy": 0.0577}, {"id": 203, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "amused", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Watched Viarmo unveil the forged Verse of King Olaf before Jarl Elisif at the Blue Palace — a masterful lie about a sleeping dragon and a cowardly king, sold as sacred history to save a bonfire festival. Elisif bought it whole, promised coin patronage, and Viarmo told Jules to seek out Jorn to restart the effigy preparations, dangling her bard induction like a carrot. Faendal turned up trailing Jules through the palace and grounds despite being dismissed twice, finally paid off and sent packing from the Bards College. Bryling quietly ordered a guard to watch the doors, fearing Thalmor mischief while the court's attention was on 'bard nonsense' — smart Nord, wasted on this simulation.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 985595.91, "x": 0.2355, "y": 0.2286, "ux": 0.3002, "uy": 0.124}, {"id": 204, "actor": "Solitude Guard", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.5, "type": "KNOWLEDGE", "content": "On duty in the Blue Palace as Viarmo petitioned Jarl Elisif to reinstate the Burning of King Olaf Festival, backed by a bard named Jules who recovered King Olaf's lost verse from the bard's tomb. Elisif was moved by the poem's mockery of Olaf and approved the festival, promising the College a reward. Thane Bryling quietly warned me to watch the doors closely during festival preparations, fearing the Thalmor might exploit the court's distraction after they stole our defense plans this morning. Also noticed a Wood Elf named Faendal wandering into the palace, chatting with Jules before leaving.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 986512.83, "x": 0.0259, "y": 0.2677, "ux": 0.3108, "uy": 0.095}, {"id": 205, "actor": "Solitude Guard", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "On patrol through the Blue Palace, I overheard Bard College headmaster Viarmo present King Olaf's Verse to Jarl Elisif and Falk Firebeard - a poem recovered from the bard's tomb claiming Olaf never fought a dragon, just captured Numinex while it slept. A Breton woman, Jules, seemed instrumental in recovering it; Viarmo spoke of inducting her as a bard once the festival resumes. Also noticed a Bosmer named Faendal wandering near the throne room, oddly out of place for a hunter type. Court business as usual, though the Olaf verse stirred some murmurs among those present.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 986512.83, "x": 0.2988, "y": 0.1573, "ux": 0.2955, "uy": 0.064}, {"id": 206, "actor": "Odar", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.3, "type": "KNOWLEDGE", "content": "Overheard a hooded stranger named Eris remark in the Blue Palace that despite Elisif being 'the seat of power in Skyrim,' she sensed only sadness from her - a stark outsider's read on our Jarl that matches my own doubts about her fitness to rule. Later, near midday, I noticed the wood elf Faendal wandering the palace, telling the Breton adventurer Jules he'd come to see the palace up close before she went off 'shouting at mountains' again. Viarmo from the Bards College mentioned a festival coming soon while passing through. Kept to my kitchen work through it all, but filed away Eris's blunt assessment of Elisif - even strangers see what I see.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 986512.83, "x": 0.4648, "y": 0.1557, "ux": 0.2582, "uy": 0.2096}, {"id": 207, "actor": "Solitude Guard", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Bryling pulled me aside at the Blue Palace and quietly warned that with the Thalmor stealing our defense plans this morning, they might strike while the court's distracted by bard business - told me to watch the doors closely during festival preparations. Meanwhile Viarmo petitioned Jarl Elisif to reinstate the Burning of King Olaf Festival, reciting a recovered verse from the Poetic Edda that convinced her to approve it. Elisif granted the College of Bards a reward for the poem. Stayed alert at my post throughout, mindful of the Thalmor threat against General Tullius earlier today.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 986512.83, "x": 0.1849, "y": 0.0373, "ux": 0.3112, "uy": 0.0081}, {"id": 208, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "joyful", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.7, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Presented King Olaf's Verse to Jarl Elisif at the Blue Palace with Viarmo - the reworked poem convinced her the Burning of King Olaf festival should proceed, and she promised patronage for the College. Viarmo told me I'd be formally inducted as a bard during the festival itself, and sent me to tell Jorn at the Bards College to finish the effigy preparations; festival starts at dusk. Faendal turned up again at the Blue Palace claiming coincidence, and I dismissed him outright this time - he took his gold and left without following further. Overheard Bryling warning a guard to watch the doors, worried the Thalmor might exploit the court's distraction after stealing Solitude's defense plans this morning.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 985595.91, "x": 0.2083, "y": 0.0524, "ux": 0.3266, "uy": 0.0862}, {"id": 209, "actor": "Solitude Guard", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Bryling pulled me aside quietly in the Blue Palace and warned me to watch the doors during the festival preparations, worried the Thalmor might strike while the court's distracted with Viarmo's bard business. Viarmo presented King Olaf's recovered verse to Jarl Elisif, convincing her to reinstate the Burning of King Olaf Festival, with a traveling Breton woman apparently instrumental in recovering the poem. Given this morning's theft of our Solitude defense plans by Thalmor spies, I take Bryling's warning seriously - stayed alert at my post through the whole affair.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 986512.83, "x": 0.2502, "y": 0.0871, "ux": 0.3034, "uy": 0.0235}, {"id": 210, "actor": "Sybille Stentor", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Viarmo of the Bards College presented Elisif with King Olaf's recovered verse from the Poetic Edda, convincing her to reinstate the Burning of King Olaf Festival. Falk Firebeard grumbled about coin-begging before the reading began, and Elisif ultimately promised the College patronage. Bryling quietly warned a guard to watch the doors during festival preparations, wary the Thalmor might exploit the distraction after this morning's theft of our defense plans. A Bosmer hunter also wandered through court gawking at the palace, harmless but out of place.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 986512.83, "x": 0.1443, "y": 0.0616, "ux": 0.3189, "uy": 0.0}, {"id": 211, "actor": "Falk Firebeard", "emotion": "content", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Viarmo of the Bards College petitioned Elisif this morning to reinstate the Burning of King Olaf Festival, presenting a newly-recovered verse from the Poetic Edda mocking Olaf as a false, cowardly king. Elisif was moved and approved both the festival and a patronage reward for the College - Viarmo credited a young Breton woman for recovering the poem. Meanwhile I overheard Bryling quietly instructing a guard to watch the doors during the festival preparations, wary the Thalmor might exploit the distraction after stealing our defense plans this morning. Court felt crowded and chaotic today - bards, petitioners, and a strange procession of odd visitors including some hooded woman and a wood elf hunter wandering through looking for the Blue Palace.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 986512.83, "x": 0.145, "y": 0.0474, "ux": 0.3067, "uy": 0.0208}, {"id": 212, "actor": "Unknown", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "On duty at the Blue Palace, I overheard Thane Bryling quietly warn me to watch the doors during Viarmo's festival petition - the Thalmor stole our defense plans for Solitude just this morning, and she fears they'll strike while court's distracted. Meanwhile Viarmo recited King Olaf's recovered verse to Jarl Elisif, convincing her to reinstate the Burning of King Olaf Festival, with the Breton woman Jules credited for recovering the poem. Stayed alert throughout, mindful of the stolen battle plans amid all the bardic pageantry.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 986512.83, "x": 0.1847, "y": 0.194, "ux": 0.3127, "uy": 0.0662}, {"id": 213, "actor": "Viarmo", "emotion": "joyful", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Elisif granted the College patronage after hearing the restored Verse of King Olaf, and I thanked her before the court. I told Jules soon after that her efforts recovering the poem earned the College's gratitude, and sent her to tell Jorn to finish the effigy preparations - the festival is back on. Overheard Thane Bryling warn a guard that Thalmor spies stole the Legion's defense plans for Solitude, urging extra watch on the palace doors during festival preparations. A busy, gratifying day at the Blue Palace.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 991643.39, "x": 0.2429, "y": 0.2547, "ux": 0.3487, "uy": 0.1325}, {"id": 214, "actor": "Erdi", "emotion": "surprised", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At the Winking Skeever, I overheard talk of the Dragonborn woman named Jules - she'd collapsed from some seizure tied to the Voice, and a man called Falion had to carry her here after seven hours unconscious. A nervous bard named Illdi asked Jules about the Thalmor Embassy hiring performers. I watched Jules buy food from Corpulus Vinius - apple pies, soup, cooked beef. Strange to be so near someone touched by dragon blood; I wonder what it's like to be swept into such adventures.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 992636.28, "x": 0.5441, "y": 0.509, "ux": 0.2763, "uy": 0.3386}, {"id": 215, "actor": "Una", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "The Blue Palace, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.3, "type": "KNOWLEDGE", "content": "Overheard Thane Bryling quietly warn a Solitude Guard to watch the doors during festival preparations, worried the Thalmor might strike while the court's attention is on bard nonsense - fresh off news they'd stolen our defense plans. Later saw a Bosmer stranger, Faendal, wandering the Blue Palace saying he wanted to see it up close after meeting a shouting woman. Viarmo mentioned the festival was coming soon. None of it my business, but I keep my ears open while I work.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 992536.74, "x": 0.436, "y": 0.039, "ux": 0.2996, "uy": 0.0274}, {"id": 216, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.55, "type": "RELATIONSHIP", "content": "Followed Jules to Solitude on my own accord, catching her at the Blue Palace and again at the Bards College, but she called me 'Fandall' and dismissed me outright - so I took my pay and stopped following, parting ways near the palace. Later I made my way to the Winking Skeever anyway, where talk buzzed about Thalmor spies stealing Legion defense plans for Solitude and an Imperial Soldier pressing Jules about it. Bard Lisette sang of the Dragonborn's coming while I watched from the common room, still stinging from being cast off after all the arrows and coin I've spent following her. Not sure why I bother chasing after a Nord who can't even get my name right.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 993417.74, "x": 0.4374, "y": 0.4993, "ux": 0.2902, "uy": 0.3171}, {"id": 221, "actor": "Jorn", "emotion": "content", "location": "The Bards College, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "The bard-to-be, Jules, told me the Burning of King Olaf festival was back on - I told her we'd gather outside the College at dusk. The next day she confirmed again and we assembled outside the Bards College for the festival. Bendt handed out sweets and candy to the crowd near the Blue Palace. Viarmo declared Jules a full-fledged member of the College afterward, and mentioned Elisif wants the Burning of King Olaf to become a weekly event.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 995938.28, "x": 0.0, "y": 0.3401, "ux": 0.2852, "uy": 0.0498}, {"id": 222, "actor": "Aia Arria", "emotion": "surprised", "location": "Some distance from Blue Palace, Solitude, Outdoors, Hold: Haafingar", "imp": 0.4, "type": "KNOWLEDGE", "content": "Word passes through the College grounds near the Blue Palace that Jules has been made a full-fledged bard by Viarmo himself, with Elisif granting a Patronage and declaring the Burning of King Olaf a weekly event. I overheard Viarmo praising her, even calling the two of them 'the only people around who aren't complete fools' - a remark I find rather presumptuous given my own standing. Bendt handed out festival sweets nearby, a rare softness from the old chef. Faendal apparently quit as Jules's follower after being curtly dismissed the day before.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 996414.78, "x": 0.0926, "y": 0.4992, "ux": 0.3017, "uy": 0.1502}, {"id": 223, "actor": "Svari", "emotion": "sad", "location": "Some distance from Blue Palace, Solitude, Outdoors, Hold: Haafingar", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "I overhear Kayd asking why adventurers don't look tough, and Minette Vinius wondering aloud why her papa won't let her see Roggvir anymore - hearing my uncle's name from her mouth makes my chest tighten. The next day Bendt hands out King Olaf's Festival sweets and candy near the palace grounds, and I linger to listen. Later I catch Viarmo telling a Breton woman she and him are the only ones who aren't fools, then wishing her well with 'may song speed you along' as she leaves.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 997112.03, "x": 0.6144, "y": 0.3507, "ux": 0.2338, "uy": 0.1297}, {"id": 224, "actor": "Kayd", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Some distance from Blue Palace, Solitude, Outdoors, Hold: Haafingar", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "I'm playing outside the Blue Palace when I spot an adventurer and say aloud that adventurers are supposed to look tougher. Minette's nearby, worrying about her Papa saying she won't see Roggvir again - she doesn't understand why. The next night, I overhear that Breton woman getting inducted into the Bards College by Viarmo, who calls her a full member and mentions Elisif wants the Burning of King Olaf held every week now. Viarmo also mentions some patronage from Elisif for her.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 997112.03, "x": 0.4081, "y": 0.2498, "ux": 0.2466, "uy": 0.1151}, {"id": 225, "actor": "Meeko", "emotion": "content", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.35, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Long stretch at the Winking Skeever in Solitude with Jules - lots of talk about stolen Legion defense plans, Thalmor spies, and General Tullius, but no fighting reached us. Jules rented a room, slept hard for seven hours after Falion carried her in from Morthal, then bought pies and soup for the pack the next day. I stayed close by Jules's leg out on the cobblestones while Dagoth Ur ranted nearby, tail thumping, content just to be near her. Later Jules became a real bard at the college with Viarmo's blessing, and the Burning of King Olaf festival got approved as a regular thing.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 997112.03, "x": 0.2277, "y": 0.6058, "ux": 0.3186, "uy": 0.2901}, {"id": 226, "actor": "Jawanan", "emotion": "surprised", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.4, "type": "KNOWLEDGE", "content": "At the Winking Skeever, I overheard an Imperial soldier tell a Breton woman - apparently the Dragonborn - that Thalmor spies stole the Legion's defense plans for Solitude, right after Bryling reported it to a guard. Corpulus Vinius kept serving customers as usual, and later sold her food while the bard Lisette sang the Dragonborn ballad over and over. Word is this Dragonborn later collapsed from the Voice's power and slept seven hours, carried back by a Redguard mage named Falion, and I heard she's now been made a full bard at the College. Strange times in Solitude - dragons, spies, and legends all mixed together while I just came in for a drink.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 998105.0, "x": 0.6371, "y": 0.1279, "ux": 0.2382, "uy": 0.3134}, {"id": 227, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.5, "type": "RELATIONSHIP", "content": "Jules woke in the Winking Skeever after Falion carried her from Morthal following another Voice-induced seizure - nearly seven hours unconscious. Lydia and I both pressed her about the toll this is taking; I told her plainly my reserves were thin from carrying her weight in worry, not just body. Jules urged me to rest, but I refused, unwilling to sleep while she courts more trouble. Later, Viarmo confirmed Jules's induction into the Bards College and Elisif's decree making the Burning of King Olaf a weekly festival - a strange note of triumph amid Solitude's rising tension, with Thalmor spies having just stolen the Legion's defense plans.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 997173.08, "x": 0.3258, "y": 0.5669, "ux": 0.3316, "uy": 0.3317}, {"id": 228, "actor": "Sorex Vinius", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Busy stretch at the Winking Skeever - my father Corpulus rented a room and sold food to a Breton woman called Jules, the one folk whisper is Dragonborn. An Imperial soldier told her Thalmor spies stole the Legion's defense plans for Solitude right from under Bryling's nose, and later I heard Jules got named a full bard of the Bards College by Viarmo himself, with Elisif granting her patronage. Lisette sang her Dragonborn ballad half a dozen times while I worked, and that madman Dagoth Ur kept shouting some nonsense order for Ash Hopper steaks and Sujamma like this was Morrowind. Strange days - war news and legends mixing in with my usual pouring of drinks.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 998105.0, "x": 0.5316, "y": 0.309, "ux": 0.2607, "uy": 0.3232}, {"id": 229, "actor": "Minette Vinius", "emotion": "content", "location": "Some distance from Blue Palace, Solitude, Outdoors, Hold: Haafingar", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Kayd wondered aloud why adventurers don't look tougher, and I found myself thinking again about Roggvir - Papa still won't explain why I'm not allowed to see him anymore. Later near the Winking Skeever, Illdi the bard offered to play a tune for me and admitted even skilled performers get nervous, quoting Dean Inge's saying that shaky hands mean you care about the song. That night near the Blue Palace, Bendt handed out King Olaf's Festival candy while Viarmo declared the stranger travelling with Lydia a full Bards College member, and Elisif apparently wants the Burning of King Olaf to become a weekly event.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 997112.03, "x": 0.4227, "y": 0.2046, "ux": 0.2508, "uy": 0.1003}, {"id": 230, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "amused", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Back at the Winking Skeever in Solitude, an Imperial soldier tells Jules the Thalmor stole Legion defense plans right out from under Bryling's nose — mortals so busy fighting each other they can't even guard paperwork. Jules officially became a bard, Viarmo confirming her induction and Elisif making the Burning of King Olaf a weekly festival, all built on the forged Verse we recovered. Eris took my offered Potion of Magicka but the item transfer glitched out — figures, even my generosity is bugged in this simulation. Jules crashed for seven hours after Falion carried her in from a Voice-induced seizure in Morthal; Lydia and Eris fussed over her like hens while I roasted the college bards' pacing and ordered a fantasy feast of Morrowind food nobody here can cook.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 997299.56, "x": 0.3391, "y": 0.4571, "ux": 0.3175, "uy": 0.3151}, {"id": 231, "actor": "Illdi", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Solitude, near the Door to The Winking Skeever, Hold: Haafingar", "imp": 0.4, "type": "RELATIONSHIP", "content": "I sought out Jules at the Winking Skeever in Solitude, nervous since I'd never met her before, only heard her name from Ataf. I introduced myself and asked about the Thalmor Embassy's interest in hiring performers - a lucrative solo opportunity I'd been offered. Jules seemed busy trading with Corpulus Vinius at the time, so our conversation felt brief and I wasn't sure she took much notice of me. Afterward I practiced a tune for Minette outside, telling her Dean Inge's advice about nervous hands meaning you care about the song.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 997112.03, "x": 0.3857, "y": 0.6215, "ux": 0.308, "uy": 0.3006}, {"id": 232, "actor": "Bendt", "emotion": "content", "location": "Some distance from Blue Palace, Solitude, Outdoors, Hold: Haafingar", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Made sweets for King Olaf's Festival and handed them out near the Blue Palace grounds, hawking 'Candy! Get your King Olaf's Festival candy!' to the gathered crowd. Bard-to-be Jules and Headmaster Viarmo were among those celebrating outside. One of the few times a year I let my sour mood slip - the festival's back on and folk deserve something sweet.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 995938.28, "x": 0.2048, "y": 0.2332, "ux": 0.2873, "uy": 0.0663}, {"id": 233, "actor": "Pantea Ateia", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At the Winking Skeever, I overheard an Imperial soldier telling that Breton adventurer Jules that Thalmor spies stole the Legion's defense plans for Solitude, straight from Bryling's own report to the guard. Lisette performed her tired Dragonborn ballad again while Corpulus fussed over renting rooms. Some crude Dunmer voice grumbled about the Bards College teaching nonsense instead of real music - insulting, given I built that institution's reputation myself. Unsettling news about the theft, though hardly surprising given how the Thalmor operate.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 998105.0, "x": 0.5088, "y": 0.3002, "ux": 0.2199, "uy": 0.3236}, {"id": 234, "actor": "Giraud Gemane", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.5, "type": "KNOWLEDGE", "content": "At the Winking Skeever in Solitude, I overheard Noster Eagle-Eye recount witnessing Roggvir's execution at the city gate for aiding Ulfric's escape after the High King's murder - grim news I passed along to Viarmo. Amid the tavern chatter, an Imperial soldier informed the woman called Jules that Thalmor spies stole Legion defense plans for Solitude, with Bryling confirming it to the guards. I also caught that strange masked Dunmer, Dagoth Ur, mocking Skyrim's bards and the College's curriculum with his usual crude irreverence. The political tension in the city feels palpable - war, sabotage, and now this execution weigh on my mind.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 998105.0, "x": 0.5954, "y": 0.3299, "ux": 0.1828, "uy": 0.3274}, {"id": 235, "actor": "Taarie", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Solitude, near the Door to The Winking Skeever, Hold: Haafingar, Outdoors", "imp": 0.2, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Standing near the Winking Skeever, I overhear the usual mix of Solitude life: Illdi practicing her bardic nerves with young Minette Vinius, that housecarl Lydia being dismissed to rest by her Breton companion, and a masked, foul-mouthed Dunmer calling himself Dagoth Ur bantering crudely with a hooded woman named Eris about potions and Vivec. Noster Eagle-Eye pestered passersby near Radiant Raiment for coin, as he always does. Later, near the Blue Palace, I catch word that Viarmo has inducted that Breton adventurer into the Bards College and secured her a patronage from Jarl Elisif herself - interesting, given my own ambitions with the Blue Palace. None of this touched me directly, but it's useful to know who's currying favor with Elisif these days.", "day": "29th of Last Seed", "gt": 1112567.76, "x": 0.5161, "y": 0.1184, "ux": 0.2613, "uy": 0.2316}, {"id": 236, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "joyful", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.75, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Inducted as a full bard at the Bards College in Solitude - Viarmo confirmed it after the Burning of King Olaf festival, with Elisif declaring it a weekly event and promising patronage. Woke to learn I'd suffered a seizure from the Voice at the Winking Skeever, unconscious for seven hours while Falion carried me to his house in Morthal before I woke back in Solitude - Eris and Lydia both worried but treated it as another cost of my path. Between festival preparations, an Imperial Soldier warned me Thalmor spies stole Solitude's defense plans, and I told Jorn at the College the festival was back on. Sent Lydia and Eris to rest at the inn, though Eris refused twice, unwilling to leave my side even exhausted.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 998043.78, "x": 0.4486, "y": 0.03, "ux": 0.2809, "uy": 0.2548}, {"id": 237, "actor": "Lydia", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "The Winking Skeever, Hold: Solitude", "imp": 0.45, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Rested at the Winking Skeever in Solitude while my Thane fell into another Voice-seizure, this time in Falion's house all the way in Morthal - he carried her back seven hours later like a sack of grain. Told Eris as much when Jules woke disoriented, half-remembering nothing. Later that night we fought through the wilderness together - a wolf and a bear went down, Meeko claiming the bear's kill, and I stood guard as always while Dagoth Ur traded barbs with Eris over who pulled their weight. A fugitive approached Jules afterward, pressing something into her hands with promises to return for it - trouble finds her wherever we go.", "day": "28th of Last Seed", "gt": 997112.03, "x": 0.5552, "y": 0.6114, "ux": 0.3706, "uy": 0.4647}, {"id": 238, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "content", "location": "Some distance from Blue Palace, Solitude, Outdoors, Hold: Haafingar", "imp": 0.3, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "I stayed on the outskirts of Solitude while Jules mingled through the King Olaf's Festival crowd near the Blue Palace - restored thanks to her efforts, by the sound of it. Watched from a distance as Viarmo, Rorlund, Silana, Una, Taarie, Illdi, and others all thanked her personally for convincing Jarl Elisif to bring the celebration back. Bendt handed out festival sweets, Sorex Vinius hawked free meat pies, and a strange blind woman named Eris spoke with Jules about Roggvir's execution - calling it unjust but necessary for the city's stability. I kept my distance from the crowd, watching Jules earn the town's gratitude while I remained just another elf on the fringes.", "day": "29th of Last Seed", "gt": 1115028.23, "x": 0.2478, "y": 0.5423, "ux": 0.3109, "uy": 0.2132}, {"id": 239, "actor": "Meeko", "emotion": "content", "location": "Skyrim Wilderness, Outdoors", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Assassin attacked Jules on the road from Dead Men's Respite - I lunged and snarled at his leg while the pack fought him off. Later at Ustengrav Outskirts, more bandits and a necromancer ambushed us - I killed the Novice Necromancer myself. Dagoth Ur mocked me for the bear kill, calling it luck, but Lydia stood up for me, saying I earned my share same as any of them. Felt good to have her back me against his sneering.", "day": "29th of Last Seed", "gt": 1120162.25, "x": 0.6848, "y": 0.6782, "ux": 0.3678, "uy": 0.5741}, {"id": 240, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Skyrim Wilderness, Outdoors", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "After Solitude's festival, we push into the wilderness and Ustengrav's outskirts, fighting bandits, a novice necromancer, and conjurers alongside Jules, Dagoth Ur, Lydia, and Meeko. I cut down a bandit myself outside Ustengrav while Dagoth Ur mocks luck and calls us all 'evolutionary dead ends' between kills. Lydia defends Meeko's kill on the bear as earned, not lucky, while Dagoth grudgingly admits Jules and I are 'pulling our weight.' Jules presses on into Ustengrav itself after barely resting, chasing whatever answers Ustengrav and the Voice still demand of her.", "day": "29th of Last Seed", "gt": 1120162.25, "x": 0.66, "y": 0.5145, "ux": 0.3989, "uy": 0.5711}, {"id": 241, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "fearful", "location": "Ustengrav, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.75, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought through the night from the roads outside Solitude to Ustengrav's outskirts and finally into the tomb itself, alongside Lydia, Eris, Dagoth Ur, and Meeko. We cut down waves of bandits, bandit outlaws, apprentice and novice conjurers, and necromancers guarding the entrance - an assassin ambushed me alone on the road first, and Meeko saved me by lunging at his leg. Dagoth Ur cracked jokes about 'evolutionary dead ends' the whole fight while Eris calmly finished off stragglers. Slept a few hours outside Ustengrav before pushing into the tomb at dawn, finally standing where the Horn of Jurgen Windcaller is said to rest.", "day": "29th of Last Seed", "gt": 1120162.25, "x": 0.7658, "y": 0.2768, "ux": 0.4157, "uy": 0.5888}, {"id": 242, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "content", "location": "Skyrim Wilderness, Outdoors", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Left Solitude's Burning of King Olaf festival behind and hit the road with Jules, Lydia, Eris, and Meeko — a bandit assassin ambushed us in the wilderness, Meeko lunging for his leg before I fried the bastard with Firebolt after threatening him with the Void and Oblivion. Called Eris an 'ash-witch' mid-fight and mocked Lydia when I ran dry and had to club someone like 'a true Nord simpleton.' A bear and a wolf went down too, Lydia crediting Meeko's kill as much as anyone's, and I needled Eris that luck's the only god in a brawl. Later at Ustengrav Outskirts, Eris solo'd two more bandits clean while I called them evolutionary dead ends — she just said their lives were expendable, use them for greater purpose. Woman speaks my language.", "day": "29th of Last Seed", "gt": 1120162.25, "x": 0.6368, "y": 0.277, "ux": 0.3918, "uy": 0.5462}, {"id": 243, "actor": "Meeko", "emotion": "fearful", "location": "Ustengrav, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought through Ustengrav in Hjaalmarch alongside Jules, Eris, and Dagoth Ur - bandits, conjurers, a necromancer, and wave after wave of draugr filled the ruin. I killed a bandit myself and helped bring down a Restless Draugr with my teeth, staying close to the pack through the chaos. Faendal turned up again too, trailing Jules like he always does, and Eris needled him about following trouble. Dagoth Ur kept ranting his strange nonsense between fights, but between all of us we cleared the place and everyone walked out alive.", "day": "30th of Last Seed", "gt": 1148424.5, "x": 0.6714, "y": 0.5883, "ux": 0.462, "uy": 0.6186}, {"id": 244, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Ustengrav, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "We push deep into Ustengrav in Hjaalmarch, clearing bandits, novice necromancers, apprentice conjurers, and a fire mage alongside Jules, Dagoth Ur, Meeko, and Faendal - who joined us again after crossing paths at the entrance. I cut down a bandit thug and apprentice fire mage myself while Dagoth Ur finished off conjurers and draugr with his usual crude commentary, once even ranting about Snow Elf ruins and asset reuse. Faendal proved steadier than I expected, holding his ground through wave after wave of restless dead, and I told him as much. Jules pressed forward relentlessly through exhaustion, and by the deeper halls we'd cleared a long procession of the dead and the arrogant alike.", "day": "30th of Last Seed", "gt": 1148617.23, "x": 0.6038, "y": 0.5066, "ux": 0.4531, "uy": 0.603}, {"id": 245, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "fearful", "location": "Ustengrav, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.65, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought deeper into Ustengrav with Eris, Dagoth Ur, Faendal, and Meeko - cut down waves of restless draugr while rival conjurers and a fire mage turned on each other and the undead. Faendal reappeared mid-crypt, joining the fight and trading barbs with Dagoth Ur over cheese and Nordic priorities. My arm went numb from crossbow kick and I'm running on fumes, but Eris kept urging me forward - 'nothing achieved without bloodshed.' The horn is close now; I can feel it.", "day": "30th of Last Seed", "gt": 1149176.38, "x": 0.7321, "y": 0.2844, "ux": 0.4689, "uy": 0.6115}, {"id": 246, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Ustengrav, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.4, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought through Ustengrav in Hjaalmarch alongside Jules, Eris, Dagoth Ur, and Meeko - draugr, conjurers, necromancers, and a fire mage fell one after another as we pushed deeper. Jules greeted me with 'doll' again, and Eris noted I've grown bolder since Riverwood; I told her a man learns quick down here or not at all. Traded gear with Jules and pressed on through the crypt's ancient halls, cheese and all - Dagoth Ur found that funnier than the draugr trying to kill us. Eris fought without hesitation, calling our fallen enemies expendable stepping stones, while I kept my bow busy and my resentment quiet.", "day": "30th of Last Seed", "gt": 1148449.3, "x": 0.5592, "y": 0.5373, "ux": 0.469, "uy": 0.5933}, {"id": 247, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "content", "location": "Ustengrav, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.35, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Grinded through Ustengrav in Hjaalmarch with Jules, Eris, Meeko, and a resurfaced Faendal — I torched a Novice Conjurer and cleaned up a Restless Draugr myself while Jules and Eris carved through the rest, including a rogue Apprentice Fire Mage and Conjurer duo who turned on each other's draugr pet. Faendal tagged along after Jules recruited him again, trading barbs with Eris about boldness and short straws. I lectured everyone on snow elf ruin erasure and Bethesda's asset-reuse cowardice, then roasted the Nords for mummifying cheese instead of inventing refrigeration. Called Faendal a twink for his bowmanship, told some draugr he'd 'burn for hitting a girl,' the usual chaos.", "day": "30th of Last Seed", "gt": 1148617.23, "x": 0.6422, "y": 0.44, "ux": 0.4623, "uy": 0.5723}, {"id": 248, "actor": "Meeko", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Ustengrav, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Cleared Ustengrav in Hjaalmarch with Jules, Eris, Dagoth Ur, and Faendal - fought through skeletons and frostbite spiders, and I brought down one of the spiders myself with my teeth. Dagoth Ur kept shouting his strange battle-cries and torching skeletons while Eris carved through them clean and calm. Jules pushed all the way to the deepest chamber only to read a note saying the horn we sought was already gone, taken by 'a friend' - felt her frustration after all that blood and bone. Everyone walked out alive again, and I stayed close to the pack the whole way.", "day": "30th of Last Seed", "gt": 1154983.67, "x": 0.6499, "y": 0.5028, "ux": 0.4816, "uy": 0.6069}, {"id": 249, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Ustengrav, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "We fought deep through Ustengrav in Hjaalmarch - I cut down a restless draugr and skeletons with Dagoth Ur, while Faendal and Meeko dealt with frostbite spiders and Jules pressed through exhaustion. Faendal warned me of my footing and I noted, dryly, that I wasn't the only one struggling to see clearly. At the end of it all, Jules read a note revealing someone calling themselves 'a friend' had already taken the horn we came for, centuries ahead of us - all that bloodshed for a relic long gone. Dagoth Ur mocked the waste with his usual crude commentary; Meeko growled at him for it.", "day": "30th of Last Seed", "gt": 1155583.85, "x": 0.6693, "y": 0.4637, "ux": 0.4746, "uy": 0.6122}, {"id": 250, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "content", "location": "Ustengrav, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.35, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Torched a whole gauntlet of skeletons through Ustengrav's depths in Hjaalmarch while Jules, Eris, Faendal, and Meeko carved and shot their way alongside me — I racked up more kills than Eris and made sure everyone knew it, 'numbers don't lie, pookie.' Faendal took down a frostbite spider clean, Eris kept slicing draugr and skeletons with cold one-liners about weakness and blindness. The whole climb was for nothing though — Jules read a note revealing some 'friend' beat us to the Horn centuries ago, an ancient loot goblin leaving what's basically a Yelp review. Meeko growled at me for shouting over Jules's disappointment, but I was too busy screaming about Fefe's new Onahole and needing Nerevar's credit card.", "day": "30th of Last Seed", "gt": 1155735.05, "x": 0.551, "y": 0.4575, "ux": 0.4853, "uy": 0.591}, {"id": 251, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "disgusted", "location": "Ustengrav, Hold: Hjaalmarch", "imp": 0.8, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought through Ustengrav with Lydia, Eris, Dagoth Ur, Faendal, and Meeko, cutting down waves of draugr and necromancers. Found the chamber of Jurgen Windcaller only to discover the Horn was already taken—left a note from an unknown 'friend'. Dagoth Ur mocked the situation while Meeko whined in disappointment; Faendal expressed bitter resignation. Exhausted but alive, we regrouped outside before returning to Riverwood.", "day": "30th of Last Seed", "gt": 1156354.35, "x": 0.8603, "y": 0.2465, "ux": 0.4485, "uy": 0.631}, {"id": 252, "actor": "Faendal", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Ustengrav in Hjaalmarch, Riverwood in Whiterun", "imp": 0.65, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Fought alongside Jules, Eris, Dagoth Ur, and Meeko through the draugr-infested halls of Ustengrav in Hjaalmarch. Exchanged barbs with Dagoth Ur over kill counts and his grotesque 'projects' with dead flesh. Felt the sting of futility when we reached the burial chamber only to learn the Horn of Jurgen Windcaller had already been taken by an unknown 'friend.' Parted ways with Jules in Riverwood after she dismissed me again—this time telling me to 'rest'—while Eris offered rare words of respect for my persistence.", "day": "30th of Last Seed", "gt": 1156354.35, "x": 0.5759, "y": 0.5503, "ux": 0.4583, "uy": 0.6124}, {"id": 253, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "amused", "location": "Sleeping Giant Inn, Hold: Riverwood", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In the Sleeping Giant Inn, Delphine revealed herself as the author of the Ustengrav note and claimed to be part of a secret group hunting the Dragonborn. She tried to recruit Jules, citing Thalmor threats and trust tests, but Jules rejected her overture. Orgnar remained indifferent, Sven bickered with him over free mead, and Eris noted the innkeeper’s hidden agenda with quiet suspicion. I stayed silent—this cult nonsense is beneath a god, but the drama’s free entertainment.", "day": "30th of Last Seed", "gt": 1163939.04, "x": 0.6483, "y": 0.1714, "ux": 0.2649, "uy": 0.9332}, {"id": 254, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Sleeping Giant Inn, Hold: Riverwood", "imp": 0.8, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In the cellar beneath the Sleeping Giant Inn in Riverwood, Delphine reveals herself as the 'friend' who took the Horn of Jurgen Windcaller centuries ago. She speaks of a secret order searching for the Dragonborn, testing Jules's trust before warning of Thalmor spies. I remain silent but attentive, noting the weight of her words and the shift in the air—this is no mere innkeeper. Jules dismisses her, but the currents of fate have undeniably turned.", "day": "30th of Last Seed", "gt": 1163939.04, "x": 0.6072, "y": 0.2916, "ux": 0.2774, "uy": 0.9524}, {"id": 255, "actor": "Meeko", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Sleeping Giant Inn in Riverwood", "imp": 0.8, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Walked with Jules into Sleeping Giant Inn in Riverwood after returning from Ustengrav and High Hrothgar. Delphine revealed she was the one who left the note, claiming to be part of a secret group watching for the Dragonborn. She showed Jules the real Horn of Jurgen Windcaller, which Arngeir later used at High Hrothgar to formally recognize Jules as Dragonborn. I stayed close through the tension, ears alert, sensing the weight of the moment despite Dagoth Ur's rants and Sven's singing.", "day": "30th of Last Seed", "gt": 1161901.51, "x": 0.4442, "y": 0.5704, "ux": 0.3278, "uy": 0.8655}, {"id": 261, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "amused", "location": "College of Winterhold, Winterhold College, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At the College of Winterhold's entrance, Faralda tested Jules's magical aptitude, demanding a display of the Thu'um after skepticism. Jules shouted 'Fus' successfully, proving her Dragonborn status and gaining entry. I stood by, amused by the elf's arrogance and the frost lingering in the air after the shout. Meeko barked at the echo, tail wagging, while Eris warned him to stay cautious around testing mages.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1236501.45, "x": 0.3709, "y": 0.5249, "ux": 0.4027, "uy": 0.2985}, {"id": 262, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "surprised", "location": "Sleeping Giant Inn in Riverwood, High Hrothgar, and College of Winterhold in Winterhold", "imp": 0.9, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Delphine in the Sleeping Giant Inn revealed she left the note in Ustengrav and claimed to be part of a group seeking the Dragonborn. She warned of Thalmor spies and offered help, but I left unconvinced. Later, Arngeir confirmed I passed the Greybeards' trials at High Hrothgar, taught me the full Unrelenting Force Shout, and formally recognized me as Dragonborn. I then traveled to Winterhold, where Faralda tested my magic at the College of Winterhold; I proved my Dragonborn status with Fus, earning entry.", "day": "30th of Last Seed", "gt": 1178326.37, "x": 0.6615, "y": 0.1096, "ux": 0.2398, "uy": 0.898}, {"id": 263, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "College of Winterhold, Winterhold College, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At the College of Winterhold's entrance, Faralda tested Jules's magical aptitude, demanding a display of the Thu'um. Jules Shouted 'Fus,' proving her Dragonborn claim, and Faralda granted her entry. Meeko reacted warily to the frost in the air, pressing close to me as I cautioned him to stay alert. The Altmer mage acknowledged our presence only with restrained disdain, but the moment marked a shift—Jules now has access to the College's arcane resources.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1236501.45, "x": 0.3821, "y": 0.4691, "ux": 0.3922, "uy": 0.2767}, {"id": 264, "actor": "Meeko", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Winterhold, Hold: Winterhold, Outdoors", "imp": 0.65, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Standing outside the College of Winterhold with Jules, Eris, and Dagoth Ur as Faralda tested Jules's Thu'um. Jules shouted 'Fus' and the air rippled with power, impressing Faralda, who then granted entry. I barked at the sudden frost in the air, pressing close to Eris while watching the mage-elf warily. The college gates opened after long silence, a victory earned not by tooth or claw, but voice.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1236204.33, "x": 0.2842, "y": 0.6456, "ux": 0.4026, "uy": 0.2879}, {"id": 265, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "", "location": "", "imp": 0.7, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "I watched Nerevar trade her street leather for the College's cheap cotton uniform and get sent off to class with Tolfdir — another elf in a robe, another lecture about magic she already breathes with her shout-lungs.", "day": null, "gt": 1784014205.3, "x": 0.5378, "y": 0.2618, "ux": 0.3654, "uy": 0.2167}, {"id": 266, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "", "location": "", "imp": 0.7, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "The innkeeper’s retreat to the cellar felt like a door closing on a lie; the air of that common room shifted the moment she left it, heavy with the promise of truths spoken only in the dark.", "day": null, "gt": 1784014205.33, "x": 0.8409, "y": 0.0843, "ux": 0.2836, "uy": 0.9015}, {"id": 267, "actor": "Meeko", "emotion": "", "location": "", "imp": 0.7, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Meeko watched the tall mage-elf lead his pack-leader across the strange stone bridge into the glowing place, the cold air still humming with the power of Jules's shout; he whined softly, a low sound of worry, as the distance between them grew.", "day": null, "gt": 1784014205.36, "x": 0.4221, "y": 0.4615, "ux": 0.4149, "uy": 0.3205}, {"id": 268, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "content", "location": "Hall of the Elements, Hold: Winterhold College", "imp": 0.65, "type": "SKILL", "content": "In the Hall of the Elements at the College of Winterhold, Tolfdir called on me to demonstrate a ward spell during the first lesson. I revealed I already knew the Lesser Ward, impressing him as I cast it effortlessly. He praised my control, contrasting me with the eager but undisciplined apprentices like J'zargo and Dagoth Ur. The moment affirmed my readiness for greater magical study despite being an outsider.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1258254.55, "x": 0.5366, "y": 0.2251, "ux": 0.9871, "uy": 0.7277}, {"id": 269, "actor": "Melker", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Hall of the Elements, Hold: Winterhold College", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Attending Tolfdir's lesson in the Hall of the Elements at the College of Winterhold. Watched Jules demonstrate a ward spell under Tolfdir's guidance while J'zargo argued for more advanced magic. Tolfdir emphasized caution and control, then assigned us to practice wards. Felt energized by the focus on defensive magic, especially knowing I can use Lesser Ward effectively.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1258254.55, "x": 0.4445, "y": 0.3825, "ux": 0.9797, "uy": 0.7099}, {"id": 270, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "amused", "location": "Hall of the Elements, Hold: Winterhold College", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In the Hall of the Elements at the College of Winterhold, Tolfdir teaches Jules and other apprentices ward spells for protection. I interrupt, asking Nerevar (Jules) if Talos was seen, escalating the chaos as J'zargo pushes to advance faster. Tolfdir insists on caution, demonstrates a ward block with Jules, and assigns practice. The class includes Brelyna Maryon, Onmund, J'zargo, and Onuja, all engaging with the lesson while I mock the academic pacing.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1258254.55, "x": 0.3132, "y": 0.4941, "ux": 0.9836, "uy": 0.6926}, {"id": 271, "actor": "Ancano", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Hall of the Elements, Hold: Winterhold College", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Walked through the Hall of the Elements after being dismissed by Mirabelle Ervine outside. Observed Tolfdir instructing new apprentices, including Jules and J'zargo, in basic ward magic. Noted Jules' prior knowledge of wards with mild interest. Remain excluded from instructional activities, reinforcing my status as an outsider despite my position.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1258254.55, "x": 0.4506, "y": 0.4597, "ux": 0.9863, "uy": 0.7153}, {"id": 272, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Hall of the Elements, Hold: Winterhold College", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In the Hall of the Elements at the College of Winterhold, Tolfdir begins instructing new apprentices in ward magic for safety. Jules demonstrates prior knowledge of ward spells, impressing Tolfdir during a live demonstration. Dagoth Ur interrupts with erratic outbursts, while J'zargo pushes for more dangerous magic, revealing impatience with caution. I stand beside Jules, sensing her tension and the volatile energy of untested mages around us.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1258254.55, "x": 0.4611, "y": 0.3704, "ux": 1.0, "uy": 0.7359}, {"id": 273, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Hall of the Elements, Hold: Winterhold College", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Walk with Jules and Mirabelle from the College courtyard to the Hall of the Elements, then toward Faralda's tower. Comment on Mirabelle’s 'only this once' remark, noting her habit of bearing extra burdens. Sense Jules's preoccupation with the Voice and the College's growing tensions. Remain wary of Ancano's presence and the weight of unspoken dangers ahead.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1264471.6, "x": 0.3767, "y": 0.4985, "ux": 0.41, "uy": 0.2592}, {"id": 274, "actor": "J'zargo", "emotion": "confident", "location": "Hall of the Elements, near the Wooden Door to Winterhold College, Hold: Winterhold College", "imp": 0.5, "type": "RELATIONSHIP", "content": "J'zargo speaks with Jules near the wooden door in the Hall of the Elements after Tolfdir's lesson. Asks if she has mastered Expert-level Destruction spells; she admits she has not. Expresses disappointment, boasts of his own confidence and ambition to become the greatest mage. Mentions leaving Elsweyr to study at Winterhold for its focus on pure magic, free from Cyrodiil's politics.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1261524.82, "x": 0.4143, "y": 0.3528, "ux": 0.9652, "uy": 0.7413}, {"id": 275, "actor": "Onuja", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Hall of the Elements, Hold: Winterhold College", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In the Hall of the Elements, Tolfdir teaches a lesson on wards for safety. Jules demonstrates a ward spell successfully, earning praise. J'zargo argues for more dangerous magic, but Tolfdir insists on caution. Later, Tolfdir announces an expedition to Saarthal for hands-on study. I observe silently, absorbing the tension between discipline and ambition.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1261524.82, "x": 0.4636, "y": 0.3332, "ux": 0.9967, "uy": 0.7184}, {"id": 276, "actor": "Jules", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Hall of the Elements, College of Winterhold", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Traded alchemical ingredients and robes with Tolfdir in the Hall of the Elements, earning 336 gold. J'zargo boasted of Saarthal and mocked restraint, while Dagoth Ur recounted absurd college memories. Mirabelle Ervine escorted me to Faralda upon request, with Eris noting the Master Wizard's guarded kindness. Overheard Enthir's warnings about forbidden research and Nirya's disdain for current leadership in the Arcanaeum.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1264685.75, "x": 0.6052, "y": 0.1003, "ux": 0.9655, "uy": 0.7444}, {"id": 277, "actor": "Sergius Turrianus", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Hall of the Elements, Hold: Winterhold College", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Walked through the Hall of the Elements while Tolfdir conducted a ward spell lesson with Jules and others. J'zargo boasted about his destructive prowess, prompting Tolfdir to caution against reckless magic. Ancano dismissed concerns with his usual arrogance, and Enthir later hinted at illicit dealings near the Arcanaeum. Dagoth Ur ranted about ancient magical mishaps, disrupting the hall with vulgar stories.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1263624.39, "x": 0.439, "y": 0.3432, "ux": 0.9672, "uy": 0.7464}, {"id": 278, "actor": "Meeko", "emotion": "content", "location": "Hall of the Elements, Hold: Winterhold College", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Walk beside Jules in the Hall of the Elements after she impressed Tolfdir with her ward spell during the lesson. Dagoth Ur rants nearby about pickles and fire tornadoes, making my ears twitch. Eris remains calm while J'zargo boasts about Saarthal, and I stay close to the pack, alert but ready.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1258254.55, "x": 0.4982, "y": 0.5065, "ux": 0.9592, "uy": 0.7197}, {"id": 279, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "amused", "location": "Hall of the Elements, College of Winterhold", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "In the Hall of the Elements at the College of Winterhold, Tolfdir teaches Jules and other apprentices ward spells while I mock the slow pace. J'zargo pushes to advance faster, eager for Saarthal, but Tolfdir insists on caution and demonstrates a ward block with Jules. I interrupt with a story about a Chimer turning into a pickle in my college days, drawing annoyed glances. The class includes Brelyna Maryon, Onmund, J'zargo, and Onuja, all tolerating my shitposting.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1264471.6, "x": 0.3844, "y": 0.4389, "ux": 0.9781, "uy": 0.7098}, {"id": 280, "actor": "Amanra Solas", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "College of Winterhold, Winterhold College, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Walking near the College courtyard, overheard Ancano press Mirabelle Ervine for explanations about College policies. Mirabelle firmly reminded him he's a guest under the Arch-Mage's tolerance. Jules arrived and was given robes and directed to Tolfdir's class. Later, Dagoth Ur shouted at Melker during a magical discharge mishap. Mirabelle later advised Jules to see Faralda for Flame Cloak training.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1258254.55, "x": 0.3511, "y": 0.4568, "ux": 0.3873, "uy": 0.2573}, {"id": 281, "actor": "Nirya", "emotion": "angry", "location": "The Arcanaeum, Hold: Winterhold College", "imp": 0.6, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Heard Jules ask Urag gro-Shub about Faralda in the Arcanaeum; later confronted Jules in the dormitory, accusing her of believing Faralda's lies without knowing the truth. Spoke with intensity, voice trembling with barely contained anger. Made clear my distrust of Faralda and anyone who listens to her.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1270166.58, "x": 0.3818, "y": 0.7248, "ux": 0.3881, "uy": 0.2852}, {"id": 282, "actor": "Nelysa", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Hall of the Elements, Hold: Winterhold College", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Observed Tolfdir's lesson in the Hall of the Elements where Jules demonstrated Steadfast Ward under his guidance. Noted J'zargo's impatience and Ancano's dismissive presence. Witnessed Jules successfully block Tolfdir's Firebolt with the ward, earning his praise. Later saw Nirya and Eris in the Arcanaeum, overhearing political murmurs and quiet wisdom. Kept walking, absorbing the mood of the College without direct involvement.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1261524.82, "x": 0.3664, "y": 0.4767, "ux": 0.9649, "uy": 0.6925}, {"id": 283, "actor": "Melker", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Hall of the Elements, Hold: Winterhold College", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Attended Tolfdir's lesson in the Hall of the Elements at the College of Winterhold. Observed Jules demonstrate a ward spell under Tolfdir's guidance while J'zargo argued for more advanced magic. Tolfdir emphasized caution and control, then assigned us to practice wards. Felt energized by the focus on defensive magic, especially knowing I can use Lesser Ward effectively.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1264471.6, "x": 0.4471, "y": 0.3964, "ux": 0.9931, "uy": 0.7078}, {"id": 284, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "amused", "location": "Saarthal Outskirts, Hold: Winterhold, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Killed Ice Wolf near Saarthal entrance while Tolfdir and Jules prepared to enter. Mocked Ancano's authority at the College and threatened to Soul Trap him earlier. Eris warned of an unfriendly presence as we approached the ruins. I'm energized and ready for whatever's inside.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1270777.81, "x": 0.4372, "y": 0.4992, "ux": 0.3699, "uy": 0.474}, {"id": 285, "actor": "Mirabelle Ervine", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "College of Winterhold, Winterhold College, Outdoors", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Escorted Jules to Faralda's tower after they requested warmth spells. Advised them to seek Faralda for Destruction training and spell purchases. Eris made a remark about courtesy and habit, to which I responded tersely. Maintained professional boundaries while fulfilling administrative duties.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1258254.55, "x": 0.323, "y": 0.6854, "ux": 0.3981, "uy": 0.2909}, {"id": 286, "actor": "Enthir", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Hall of the Elements, Hold: Winterhold College", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Overheard J'zargo boast about Saarthal and his mastery of destruction magic in the Hall of the Elements. Noted Ancano's dismissive attitude toward students and Tolfdir's warning to J'zargo about recklessness. Later reminded a passing mage that unapproved magical work is best kept quiet—and directed them to me for discreet procurement. Maintained cover while reinforcing my role as the College's silent supplier.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1264685.75, "x": 0.5504, "y": 0.1656, "ux": 0.9574, "uy": 0.7568}, {"id": 287, "actor": "Tolfdir", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Saarthal, Hold: Winterhold", "imp": 0.85, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "At Saarthal, Jules triggered an ancient mechanism by removing an amulet from the wall, sealing herself inside a chamber. A resonance occurred between her and the wall, suggesting the amulet was a bloodline key. Eris interpreted the event as a response to Jules's blood, while Tolfdir noted the strange magical resonance and urged further testing. Later, Nerien of the Psijic Order manifested, warning of impending danger and affirming Jules's unique role, which Tolfdir sensed faintly but did not witness directly. The event deepened his concern and curiosity about the ruins' hidden mechanisms and their connection to Jules.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1281339.1, "x": 0.4176, "y": 0.6831, "ux": 0.3855, "uy": 0.3413}, {"id": 288, "actor": "Myvrana Giladren", "emotion": "neutral", "location": "Hall of the Elements, College of Winterhold", "imp": 0.5, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Observed Tolfdir's lesson in the Hall of the Elements where he taught restoration wards to new apprentices, including Jules. Jules demonstrated prior knowledge of the Lesser Ward spell during a live demonstration. Later saw Urag gro-Shub enforcing strict rules about book handling in the Arcanaeum. Briefly acknowledged Jules with a greeting upon entering the library.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1261524.82, "x": 0.4318, "y": 0.5638, "ux": 0.9902, "uy": 0.7047}, {"id": 289, "actor": "Meeko", "emotion": "concerned", "location": "Saarthal, Hold: Winterhold", "imp": 0.9, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Jules retrieves the final Gauldur Amulet fragment from Jyrik Gauldurson's corpse in Saarthal's depths after a fierce battle against the powerful draugr lord. Tolfdir witnesses the magical stone's emergence and insists Jules report the discovery to Arch-Mage Savos Aren immediately. The air hums with ancient power as the party stands amidst the ruins' sealed chambers, the weight of the find settling in.", "day": "31st of Last Seed", "gt": 1270635.51, "x": 0.5244, "y": 0.5771, "ux": 0.3977, "uy": 0.3431}, {"id": 290, "actor": "Dagoth Ur", "emotion": "", "location": "", "imp": 0.7, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "I watched the old man's eyes widen as the wall hummed back at Nerevar's touch, the resonance of her blood and that trinket unlocking deeper secrets than his dusty cataloguing could ever dream of — the Dwemer's true arrogance, laid bare for the taking.\nTolfdir's senile disbelief at the Psijic ghost's warning was delicious — the old goat couldn't even see the spectral omen hovering right in front of him while Nerevar laid it out plain, the air still tasting of ancient arrogance and imminent, dusty danger.\nI watched the old goat leave Nerevar to face the whispers of the wall alone, his academic cowardice a far greater danger than any dusty draugr yet to stir.", "day": null, "gt": 1784016475.91, "x": 0.5782, "y": 0.2132, "ux": 0.4642, "uy": 0.4918}, {"id": 291, "actor": "Eris", "emotion": "", "location": "", "imp": 0.7, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "The stone remembered her touch, humming with a resonance that felt both ancient and deeply personal—a door opening not by lock, but by lineage. I followed Tolfdir deeper, the air growing colder and heavier with a power that his scholarly curiosity could not fully measure.\nTolfdir’s scholarly skepticism was a thin veil against the truth; I felt the chill of the apparition’s passing like a breath from a tomb, and knew the Psijics’ warning was a thread in a tapestry far older than his doubts.\nThe stone's resonance became a warning hum, and I felt the chill of ancient wards breaking before I heard Tolfdir's scholarly alarm; the danger was never lost, merely waiting.", "day": null, "gt": 1784016475.96, "x": 0.7495, "y": 0.0, "ux": 0.2929, "uy": 0.8218}, {"id": 292, "actor": "Meeko", "emotion": "", "location": "", "imp": 0.7, "type": "EXPERIENCE", "content": "Meeko watched the pack-leader's hand touch the cold stone, his ears pricking at the strange hum that followed and the way the old mage's scent shifted from worry to sharp curiosity.\nMeeko’s nose twitched at the sudden, sharp scent of surprise and disbelief from the old mage, and he pressed closer to Jules’s leg, sensing a new, unseen danger in the air that the pack-leader had scented first.\nMeeko pressed against Jules's leg as the old mage's scent sharpened with a sudden, bright alarm, the pack-leader's discovery of the humming stone now filling the air with a tension that promised unseen teeth in the dark ahead.", "day": null, "gt": 1784016476.01, "x": 0.5243, "y": 0.3437, "ux": 0.4276, "uy": 0.3435}], "edges": [[0, 7, 0.907], [0, 116, 0.901], [1, 9, 0.891], [1, 79, 0.875], [2, 3, 0.934], [2, 5, 0.939], [3, 5, 0.929], [3, 93, 0.892], [4, 6, 0.955], [4, 9, 0.94], [6, 9, 0.949], [7, 8, 0.935], [7, 127, 0.906], [8, 9, 0.905], [9, 83, 0.881], [9, 113, 0.91], [10, 26, 0.873], [10, 109, 0.886], [10, 131, 0.889], [11, 35, 0.892], [11, 116, 0.891], [12, 79, 0.898], [12, 111, 0.898], [13, 14, 0.9], [13, 16, 0.874], [14, 15, 0.904], [14, 16, 0.928], [15, 16, 0.96], [17, 21, 0.822], [17, 115, 0.816], [18, 27, 0.901], [18, 136, 0.897], [19, 27, 0.906], [19, 32, 0.91], [20, 22, 0.83], [20, 24, 0.874], [20, 31, 0.871], [20, 34, 0.926], [20, 35, 0.912], [21, 115, 0.884], [21, 116, 0.859], [22, 34, 0.838], [23, 34, 0.862], [23, 35, 0.854], [24, 34, 0.912], [25, 34, 0.896], [25, 35, 0.91], [26, 129, 0.865], [27, 29, 0.937], [27, 32, 0.